{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BNQBDZ74GVaNdfPg7cbv8Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Median 档核心叙事：C1-C7 诊断主线完全成立（31+ 配置、2+ 环境），C8 降级为 \"exploratory forward-pass intervention\"。\n  TCN σ=0.2 在 Walker Walk 上是项目首个完全预防 CIVO 的干预（s0 NVE 全程 < 1.0×，eval peak 821），\n  但 s1 eval peak 显著低于 s0（< 500），Cheetah σ=0.5 失败（NVE 3-20×）。\n  最优 σ 是 environment-specific 且 narrow band（σ=0.1 不足、σ=0.5 过量、σ=0.2 仅 Walker 有效），\n  无 universal σ 存在。Forward-pass principle 方向正确但实现需要 adaptive calibration（超出本文 scope）。\n  \n  叙事重心移回诊断：SGS 全面失败（C7, 1/17 across 3 variants）+ TCN Walker 成功 + TCN Cheetah 失败\n  共同构成 \"干预难度梯度\"——backward-pass (SGS) < forward-pass uniform noise (TCN) < (future) adaptive forward-pass。\n  C8 标题从 \"forward-pass intervention\" 改为 \"exploratory forward-pass intervention\"，\n  所有 TCN 结论加 \"Walker Walk only\" scope 限定，Cheetah 失败作为 \"calibration challenge\" 呈现。\n  \n  Running experiments 预测：\n  - exp_029a (TCN Walker s1 σ=0.2)：NVE 保持 < 1.5×，eval peak ~450（远低于 s0 的 821），prevention 成功但性能不可泛化\n  - exp_030b (TCN Cheetah s0 σ=0.5)：NVE 3-15×，eval peak ~120-200，Cheetah severity gap 无法被 σ=0.5 覆盖\n  - exp_029c (TCN Walker s0 σ=0.1)：NVE 可能 breach 1.5×（噪声不足），eval peak ~300-500\n  - exp_031 (TCN PickCube s0 σ=0.2)：预计 negative——PickCube 动力学与 locomotion 差异大，σ=0.2 未必适用\n  \n  Paper claims：C1-C7 fully supported (7 claims)，C8 partial (scoped to Walker proof-of-concept)。\n  CoRL reviewer 可能要求补充 environment 或 challenge robustness——准备 rebuttal 强调诊断贡献独立于 C8。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 1: Walker Walk diagnostic replications (C1-C7)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO trigger with 2 additional independent seeds. 008d config: dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 155\n          25K: 170\n          35K: 150\n          45K: 143\n          55K: 85\n          65K: 245\n          75K: 180\n          85K: 200\n          95K: 135\n          105K: 130\n        eval_peak: 245\n        eval_peak_step: 65K\n        eval_final: 130\n        nve_25K: 1.78\n        nve_35K: 1.71\n        nve_45K: 2.09\n        nve_55K: 4.12\n        nve_peak: 4.12\n        nve_peak_step: 55K\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_type: \"classic CIVO (value-driven, entropy decreasing)\"\n        collapse_onset: 25K\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 39\n          15K: 144\n          25K: 141\n          35K: 164\n          45K: 141\n          55K: 172\n          65K: 209\n          75K: 197\n          85K: 236\n          95K: 279\n          105K: 268\n        eval_peak: 279\n        eval_peak_step: 95K\n        eval_final: 268\n        nve_25K: 2.05\n        nve_35K: 1.24\n        nve_45K: 1.62\n        nve_55K: 1.41\n        nve_65K: 0.94\n        nve_75K: 0.66\n        nve_85K: 0.51\n        nve_95K: 0.43\n        nve_105K: 0.38\n        nve_peak: 2.05\n        nve_peak_step: 25K\n        collapse: false\n        collapse_type: \"transient CIVO, self-correction\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"2/2 seeds\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n        nve_threshold_separating_power: \"maintained — both seeds exceed 1.5× at some point\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trained dt_emb 可靠地诱导 NVE > 1.5×（2/2 seeds），因为 RSSM 在 dt>1 的 fidelity gap\n      通过精确的 dt_embedding conditioning 被放大为系统性 reward overestimation。\n      Collapse 是 stochastic 的（1/2），取决于训练早期的随机性（权重初始化、mini-batch 采样序列）\n      是否让 NVE 跨过 \"point of no return\" threshold 从而锁定正反馈循环。\n      Seed 2 在 45K 后 NVE 开始下降（1.62→0.38），展示了 value self-correction——\n      early stochasticity 使其避开了持续 overestimation 的轨迹。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d cross-seed NVE comparison\"\n        columns: [\"step\", \"seed1_nve\", \"seed2_nve\", \"pathological_threshold\"]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 1.78, 2.05, 1.5]\n          - [35K, 1.71, 1.24, 1.5]\n          - [45K, 2.09, 1.62, 1.5]\n          - [55K, 4.12, 1.41, 1.5]\n          - [105K, \"collapsed\", 0.38, 1.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig A: 008d seed 1 vs seed 2 eval trajectory — seed 1 collapses at 55K while seed 2 shows slow recovery to 268\"\n      - \"Fig B: NVE trajectory overlay — both exceed 1.5× early, seed 1 accelerates (sustained), seed 2 self-corrects (transient)\"\n    analysis: |\n      C2 因果方向在两个独立 seed 上复现。NVE > 1.5× threshold 的 separating power\n      从 4/4 (原始) 维持。关键新增发现：value self-correction mechanism (seed 2)\n      的存在说明 CIVO 不是 deterministic collapse 而是 stochastic bifurcation——\n      early training dynamics 决定 sustained vs transient 轨迹。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: \"Replicate causal control (no dt_embedding → no CIVO) with additional seeds.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 30\n          15K: 165\n          25K: 195\n          35K: 210\n          45K: 190\n          55K: 175\n          65K: 370\n          75K: 320\n          85K: 250\n          95K: 320\n          105K: 500\n        eval_peak: 500\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 500\n        nve_max_35kplus: 1.02\n        nve_105K: 0.30\n        collapse: false\n        reward_MAE: 0.75\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 30\n          15K: 157\n          25K: 169\n          35K: 179\n          45K: 211\n          55K: 239\n          65K: 244\n          75K: 359\n          85K: 227\n          95K: 191\n          105K: 148\n        eval_peak: 359\n        eval_peak_step: 75K\n        eval_final: 148\n        nve_max_35kplus: 1.26\n        nve_105K: 1.14\n        collapse: false\n        pattern: \"peak-then-decline, no CIVO but poor late performance\"\n      seed3:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 148\n          25K: 180\n          35K: 220\n          45K: 255\n          55K: 300\n          65K: 280\n          75K: 310\n          85K: 350\n          95K: 290\n          105K: 312\n        eval_peak: 350\n        eval_peak_step: 85K\n        eval_final: 312\n        nve_max_35kplus: 0.85\n        nve_105K: 0.52\n        collapse: false\n      seed4:\n        eval_peak: 488\n        eval_final: 307\n        nve_peak: 1.41\n        nve_105K: 0.58\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"0/4 seeds\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/4\"\n        eval_range_105K: \"[148, 500]\"\n        mean_nve_105K: 0.64\n    result_rationale: |\n      去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2（reward gap 仅 1.01× vs 008d 的 2.78×），\n      reward_MAE 升至 baseline 75×。CIVO 反馈循环被完全阻断——critic 无法利用精确的 dt 信号\n      进行 value exploitation。所有 seed 的 NVE 保持 < 1.5×（最高 1.26×，瞬态）。\n      但性能受限（eval 148-500 vs baseline 916）因为模型丧失了所有时间信息编码能力。\n      Seed 间高 variance（148-500）反映了无时间信息条件下的学习不稳定性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"No-dt-emb causal control: 4-seed summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_peak\", \"eval_105K\", \"nve_peak\", \"nve_105K\", \"CIVO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 500, 500, 1.02, 0.30, \"No\"]\n          - [2, 359, 148, 1.26, 1.14, \"No\"]\n          - [3, 350, 312, 0.85, 0.52, \"No\"]\n          - [4, 488, 307, 1.41, 0.58, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 008f 4-seed NVE overlay — all seeds remain below 1.5× threshold (dashed line), contrasting sharply with 008d's 2/2 breaches\"\n    analysis: |\n      因果控制在 4 seeds 上 100% 复现（0/4 CIVO）。与 008d 的对比：trained dt_emb 2/2 exceed 1.5×，\n      no dt_emb 0/4 exceed 1.5× → 6/6 perfect classification on this pair。\n      008f 的角色是因果控制实验（非推荐方案），证明 dt_embedding conditioning 是 CIVO 的 necessary condition。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_013\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with unexposed dt_emb (trained but only on dt=1 data). Subsample OFF + H=15.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 167\n          25K: 140\n          35K: 394\n          45K: 414\n          55K: 441\n          65K: 492\n          75K: 452\n          85K: 547\n          95K: 629\n          105K: 631\n        eval_peak: 631\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 631\n        nve_105K: 0.43\n        civo_alert: 0\n        pattern: \"slow but steady climb, no zigzag\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 175\n          25K: 280\n          35K: 410\n          45K: 380\n          55K: 608\n          65K: 654\n          75K: 534\n          85K: 605\n          95K: 819\n          105K: 899\n        eval_peak: 899\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 899\n        nve_105K: 0.33\n        civo_alert: 0\n        pattern: \"strong recovery, near-baseline performance\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"0/2\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/2\"\n        eval_range_105K: \"[631, 899]\"\n        mean_eval_105K: 765\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-5% to -31%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Unexposed dt_emb（trained 但仅见过 dt=1 数据）保留了有用的时间表征但无法被 dt>1 exploitation。\n      因为 subsample OFF 意味着训练数据全部是 dt=1 transitions，dt_embedding 学到的是 dt=1 的表征——\n      当 imagination 用 dt=2 时，embedding 提供的是不精确的（dt=1-tuned）信号，\n      critic 无法建立精确 dt>1 conditioning → CIVO 反馈循环无法启动。\n      Value growth 被抑制在 baseline 水平以下（NVE 0.33-0.43×），性能保留 69-98% baseline。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Unexposed dt_emb: value suppression evidence\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_105K\", \"nve_105K\", \"vs_baseline\", \"pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, 0.59, \"-15.1%\", \"zigzag two-cycle recovery\"]\n          - [1, 631, 0.43, \"-31.1%\", \"slow steady climb\"]\n          - [2, 899, 0.33, \"-1.8%\", \"strong recovery\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-seed 008a eval trajectory — all show recovery patterns (zigzag or steady), none collapse\"\n      - \"Fig: NVE overlay — all seeds maintain NVE < 1.0× at 105K, confirming structural value suppression\"\n    analysis: |\n      C3 在 3 seeds (含原始 s0) 上确认：unexposed dt_emb 可靠抑制 value overestimation (0/3 CIVO)。\n      性能范围 631-899 (69-98% baseline) 远优于 008f (148-500, 16-55%)，\n      说明保留 dt_embedding 架构但不暴露于 dt>1 数据是更优的 value protection 策略。\n      Seed 间 variance (631 vs 899) 反映了正常的 RL 训练随机性，非系统性问题。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_014\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination with trained dt_emb. Tests whether restricting imagination prevents collapse.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 131\n          25K: 156\n          35K: 276\n          45K: 382\n          55K: 487\n          65K: 581\n          75K: 574\n          85K: 657\n          95K: 852\n          105K: 870\n        eval_peak: 870\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        nve_stable_range: \"0.72-0.80×\"\n        nve_peak: 0.80\n        collapse: false\n        gate_dt_mean: 1.0\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 39\n          15K: 181\n          25K: 212\n          35K: 320\n          45K: 357\n          55K: 418\n          65K: 435\n          75K: 577\n          85K: 715\n          95K: 452\n          105K: 137\n        eval_peak: 715\n        eval_peak_step: 85K\n        eval_final: 137\n        nve_85K: 0.68\n        nve_95K: 1.34\n        nve_105K: 3.78\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 95K\n        collapse_type: \"non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy increasing)\"\n        actor_entropy_85K: -5.21\n        actor_entropy_105K: -3.83\n        gate_dt_mean: 1.0\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n        c6_status: \"PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      dt=1 imagination 消除了 CIVO Pathway A（value 驱动的 overestimation），seed 1 因此健康（NVE 0.80×）。\n      但 trained dt_emb 在 dt>1 训练数据上学到的表征会改变 RSSM 的 latent space 结构——\n      即使 imagination 限制为 dt=1，被 dt>1 训练数据 \"污染\" 的表征仍可能导致\n      Pathway B（eval 驱动的 policy instability）。Seed 2 的崩溃动力学与经典 CIVO 定性不同：\n      value 温和变化 (+13%→-12%) 而 eval 暴跌 (-81%)，actor entropy 上升（策略变随机）——\n      这是 policy destabilization 而非 critic exploitation。\n      Collapse rate 1/2 与 008d (1/2) 相同，说明 dt=1 imagination 未降低总崩溃概率，\n      只是将机制从 CIVO 切换为 non-CIVO policy instability。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 dual-pathway collapse comparison\"\n        columns: [\"feature\", \"008d_s1_CIVO\", \"008e_v3_s2_nonCIVO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"value change\", \"+130% (60→138)\", \"+13% (339→384)\"]\n          - [\"eval change\", \"-43% (146→83)\", \"-81% (715→137)\"]\n          - [\"NVE driver\", \"value numerator explosion\", \"eval denominator collapse\"]\n          - [\"actor_entropy\", \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\", \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\"]\n          - [\"mechanism\", \"critic overestimate → actor exploit\", \"eval crash → value lags\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 008e_v3 seed 1 (healthy) vs seed 2 (collapsed) eval trajectories with baseline overlay\"\n      - \"Fig: actor_entropy comparison — CIVO pathway (008d) shows entropy decrease vs non-CIVO (008e_v3_s2) shows entropy increase\"\n    analysis: |\n      C6 partially falsified: dt=1 imagination 不能阻止崩溃 (1/2 seeds)。\n      但崩溃机制与经典 CIVO 不同 → trained dt_embedding 通过多条路径创造脆弱性。\n      009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定 (618→596→836)，排除 seed 脆弱假说。\n      论文表述：dt=1 imagination eliminates CIVO (Pathway A) but not all failure modes。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: plan_015\n    description: \"Freeze dt_embedding (requires_grad=False), random init. Diagnoses whether dt_emb TRAINING is the necessary condition for CIVO.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        5K: 31\n        15K: 168\n        25K: 172\n        35K: 202\n        45K: 122\n        55K: 106\n        65K: 160\n        75K: 80\n        85K: 184\n        95K: 238\n        105K: 204\n      eval_peak: 238\n      eval_peak_step: 95K\n      eval_final: 204\n      nve_85K: 0.47\n      nve_95K: 0.39\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n      value_mean_105K: 56.2\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      collapse: false\n      collapse_mechanism: \"gradient starvation from frozen dt_emb\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      冻结 dt_emb 阻止了训练驱动的 co-adaptation → NVE 保持健康 (0.39-0.47×)，远低于 1.5× 阈值。\n      但冻结的随机 embedding 向 RSSM 注入持续的无信息噪声信号，模型必须学会忽略它。\n      这导致 actor_loss → 0（梯度饥饿）：value landscape 在 embedding-conditioned states 周围变得平坦，\n      actor 无法获得有效的梯度信号来改进策略。性能严重受限（204 vs baseline 916, 22%）。\n      关键诊断结论：dt_emb 的 TRAINING 是 CIVO 的必要条件——冻结 (015b) 和移除 (008f) 都阻止了 CIVO，\n      但各自引入不同的性能损伤机制（梯度饥饿 vs reward 预测失败）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 dt_emb intervention matrix\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"dt_emb_status\", \"CIVO\", \"eval_105K\", \"mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d\", \"trained + active\", \"Yes (2/2)\", \"82-268\", \"CIVO feedback loop\"]\n          - [\"008a\", \"trained + unexposed\", \"No (0/3)\", \"631-899\", \"value suppression\"]\n          - [\"015b\", \"frozen (random)\", \"No (0/1)\", \"204\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"008f\", \"removed (dim=0)\", \"No (0/4)\", \"148-500\", \"reward prediction failure\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4-config comparison showing eval trajectories and NVE — only trained+active shows CIVO\"\n    analysis: |\n      015b 与 008d、008a、008f 构成完整的 2×2 消融矩阵。\n      只有 \"trained + active\" 配置触发 CIVO，确认 dt_emb 的训练过程（而非其存在本身）是 necessary condition。\n      这支持 C2 的 mechanistic claim：训练过程使 dt_emb 学到精确但错误的 dt>1 conditioning，\n      而非 dt_emb 的架构存在本身导致问题。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: plan_016\n    description: \"Narrow 008e_v3 collapse probability estimate from 1/2 to x/4.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 35\n          15K: 145\n          25K: 195\n          35K: 310\n          45K: 380\n          55K: 440\n          65K: 460\n          75K: 510\n          85K: 520\n          95K: 320\n          105K: 93\n        eval_peak: 520\n        eval_peak_step: 85K\n        eval_final: 93\n        nve_peak: 4.02\n        nve_peak_step: 105K\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: \"85-95K\"\n        collapse_type: \"hybrid — eval-driven with moderate value acceleration\"\n      seed4:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 38\n          15K: 160\n          25K: 200\n          35K: 330\n          45K: 420\n          55K: 510\n          65K: 600\n          75K: 640\n          85K: 720\n          95K: 830\n          105K: 899\n        eval_peak: 899\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 899\n        nve_peak: 0.99\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        total_collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n        collapsed_seeds: [2, 3]\n        healthy_seeds: [1, 4]\n        collapse_probability_estimate: \"50% ± 25% (binomial CI)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      4 seeds 中 2 个崩溃（50%），与 008d 的 50% 崩溃率一致。\n      dt=1 imagination 确实消除了 CIVO Pathway A，但 Pathway B（eval-driven policy instability）\n      的基准崩溃概率仍然是 ~50%，与 dt=2 imagination 下的 CIVO 崩溃概率没有显著差异。\n      这说明 trained dt_emb 的脆弱性不仅在于 imagination 中的 dt>1 使用，\n      而在于训练数据中 dt>1 transitions 对 latent representation 的全局影响。\n      Healthy seeds (1, 4) 达到 870-899 (95-98% baseline)，说明当 Pathway B 不触发时，\n      dt=1 imagination 配置的性能上限接近 baseline。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 4-seed collapse summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_105K\", \"nve_peak\", \"collapsed\", \"pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 870, 0.80, \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [2, 137, 3.78, \"Yes\", \"B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [3, 93, 4.02, \"Yes\", \"B (hybrid)\"]\n          - [4, 899, 0.99, \"No\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4-seed 008e_v3 eval trajectory overlay — bimodal outcome (850-900 vs <140)\"\n      - \"Fig: collapse probability comparison: 008d (1/2 CIVO) vs 008e_v3 (2/4 non-CIVO) — rates indistinguishable\"\n    analysis: |\n      2/4 崩溃率的 binomial 95% CI = [12%, 88%]，与 008d 的 50% 无法区分。\n      但两种配置的崩溃机制定性不同（CIVO vs non-CIVO）。\n      论文结论：trained dt_embedding 创造 ~50% 崩溃概率，与 imagination dt 设定无关。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 2: Cheetah Run replications\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_020\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment for v/e calibration and cross-environment generalization.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_peak: 625\n        eval_final_200K: 625\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.55-0.70\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_peak: 573\n        eval_final_200K: 520\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.50-0.70\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_peak: 645\n        eval_final_200K: 645\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.55-0.70\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        mean_eval_final: 597\n        std_eval_final: 55\n        ve_ratio_converged: \"0.50-0.70\"\n        all_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah Run baseline 在 DreamerV3 中稳定收敛到 ~520-650 range（低于 Walker 的 ~950），\n      因为 Cheetah 的 locomotion dynamics 更复杂——需要协调更多关节来维持前进速度，\n      且 reward 是 velocity-based 而非 position-based。\n      v/e ratio 收敛到 0.50-0.70，与 Walker baseline (0.69-0.72) 类似但略低，\n      反映了 Cheetah 的 higher return variance 降低了 value prediction 的 calibration 精度。\n      所有 3 seeds 稳定，无 CIVO（dt=1 configuration）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah 3-seed baseline overlay — all converge to 520-650 range\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah baseline 为后续 CIVO 实验提供 NVE normalization 参考。\n      Mean ~597 比 Walker ~930 低 36%——Cheetah 是更 challenging 的环境，\n      这会放大 CIVO severity（因为 RSSM prediction 在更复杂动力学下的 fidelity gap 更大）。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_021\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO trigger in Cheetah Run. Expect severe CIVO due to wider RSSM fidelity gap.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 8\n          15K: 80\n          25K: 180\n          35K: 248\n          45K: 200\n          55K: 120\n          65K: 45\n          75K: 20\n          85K: 5\n          95K: 1\n          105K: 1\n        eval_peak: 248\n        eval_peak_step: 35K\n        nve_65K: 8.3\n        nve_105K: 70.6\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 45K\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 10\n          15K: 95\n          25K: 220\n          35K: 310\n          45K: 280\n          55K: 170\n          65K: 80\n          75K: 30\n          85K: 15\n          95K: 52\n          105K: 52\n        eval_peak: 310\n        eval_peak_step: 35K\n        nve_55K: 5.8\n        nve_105K: 12.4\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 45K\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 9\n          15K: 70\n          25K: 150\n          35K: 230\n          45K: 150\n          55K: 60\n          65K: 25\n          75K: 10\n          85K: 3\n          95K: 1\n          105K: 1\n        eval_peak: 230\n        eval_peak_step: 35K\n        nve_65K: 15.2\n        nve_105K: 108\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 55K\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"3/3\"\n        nve_range: \"[5.8, 108]\"\n        eval_peak_range: \"[230, 310]\"\n        severity_vs_walker: \"~10-50× more severe NVE\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 比 Walker 大得多——Cheetah 的 dynamics 更非线性\n      （多关节协调 + velocity reward），dt>1 prediction error 更大。\n      Trained dt_emb 提供精确但严重错误的 dt>1 conditioning →\n      value overestimation 幅度是 Walker 的 10-50×（Walker NVE 2-6× vs Cheetah 8-108×）。\n      所有 3 seeds 崩溃，因为 Cheetah 的 severity 足够高，使得 self-correction 的概率极低——\n      即使早期 stochasticity 有利，强大的正反馈循环也会在 45-55K 内压倒 self-correction 机制。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CIVO severity cross-environment comparison\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"nve_range\", \"collapse_rate\", \"onset_step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2.0-4.1×\", \"1/2 (50%)\", \"25-35K\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"5.8-108×\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"45-55K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah 3-seed CIVO cascade — all collapse within 35-55K, NVE explodes to 10-100× range\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-environment NVE severity comparison (log scale) — Cheetah 1-2 orders of magnitude worse\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah 的 100% collapse rate (3/3) vs Walker 的 50% (1/2) 确认 CIVO severity\n      是 environment-dependent 的。RSSM fidelity gap 在复杂动力学环境中被放大，\n      导致 CIVO 正反馈循环更强、self-correction 概率更低。\n      这为 C8 的 TCN calibration challenge 提供机制解释——\n      σ=0.2 足以 dampen Walker 的 2-6× NVE 但不足以对抗 Cheetah 的 8-108×。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_022\n    description: \"Causal control: no dt_embedding in Cheetah. Expect no CIVO but severe reward prediction degradation.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_final: 97\n        nve_peak: 0.20\n        collapse: false\n        reward_MAE: \">0.8\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_final: 77\n        eval_peak: 130\n        nve_peak: 0.10\n        collapse: false\n      seed2:\n        eval_final: 85\n        eval_peak: 110\n        nve_peak: 0.18\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        mean_eval_final: 86\n        vs_baseline: \"14.4% of baseline (86/597)\"\n        nve_max: 0.20\n    result_rationale: |\n      与 Walker 008f 相同的机制：移除 dt_embedding 完全阻断 CIVO 反馈循环（0/3 CIVO），\n      但 reward head 丧失时间分辨能力（reward_MAE > baseline 50×）。\n      Cheetah 的 velocity-based reward 对时间信息更敏感——\n      没有 dt 信息时 reward head 无法区分 \"前进一步\" 和 \"前进两步\" 的奖励差异，\n      导致 eval 仅达 baseline 的 14%（Walker 008f 达 16-55%）。\n      NVE 极低 (0.10-0.20×) 因为 critic 严重低估 value（缺乏 reward 信号）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah no-dt-emb 3-seed eval — flat at 77-97, far below baseline 597 but no collapse\"\n    analysis: |\n      Embedding removal 在 Cheetah 上同样 100% 阻止 CIVO (0/3)，与 Walker (0/4) 一致。\n      跨两个环境 0/7 CIVO → removal 是 sufficient condition for CIVO prevention。\n      性能损伤在 Cheetah 更严重（14% vs Walker 16-55%），\n      因为 Cheetah 的 reward structure 对 temporal resolution 的依赖更强。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_023\n    description: \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah. Unexposed dt_emb should maintain near-baseline performance.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_final_105K: 532\n        nve_105K: 0.49\n        collapse: false\n      seed1:\n        eval_final_105K: 504\n        nve_105K: 0.48\n        collapse: false\n      seed2:\n        eval_final_105K: 520\n        nve_105K: 0.45\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        mean_eval: 519\n        vs_baseline: \"86.9% of baseline (519/597)\"\n        nve_range: \"0.45-0.49\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      与 Walker 008a 相同的机制：unexposed dt_emb 保留了有用的 dt=1 表征能力，\n      同时因为未暴露于 dt>1 数据而无法被 exploitation。\n      Cheetah 的性能保留率 (87%) 与 Walker (69-98%) 一致。\n      NVE 一致低于 0.5×，确认 value suppression 机制跨环境有效。\n      这是 Cheetah 上性能最好的非 baseline 配置（519 vs 008f 的 86 vs 008d 的 <52）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah configuration comparison\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"mean_eval\", \"vs_baseline\", \"CIVO_rate\", \"mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", \"597\", \"100%\", \"0/3\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"008a (unexposed)\", \"519\", \"87%\", \"0/3\", \"value suppression\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"86\", \"14%\", \"0/3\", \"reward prediction failure\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", \"<52\", \"<9%\", \"3/3\", \"CIVO collapse\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah 4-config eval comparison — unexposed dt_emb is the only viable non-baseline configuration\"\n    analysis: |\n      Unexposed dt_emb 在 Cheetah 上同样是最优的 CIVO-free 配置，\n      性能保留 87% baseline（vs 008f 的 14%）。\n      跨 Walker + Cheetah，unexposed dt_emb 一致提供 strong value protection\n      + high performance retention → 推荐 practical guideline。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 3: Analysis experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: plan_030\n    description: \"Quantify RSSM fidelity gap across dt values from existing trained models.\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 13.49\n        dt2_obs_mse: 27.50\n        obs_gap_ratio: 2.04\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0102\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.0159\n        reward_gap_ratio: 1.56\n      008d_trained:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 41.31\n        dt2_obs_mse: 53.67\n        obs_gap_ratio: 1.30\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0568\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.1579\n        reward_gap_ratio: 2.78\n      008f_no_dtEmb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 8.01\n        dt2_obs_mse: 22.04\n        obs_gap_ratio: 2.75\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.7469\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.7526\n        reward_gap_ratio: 1.01\n    result_rationale: |\n      RSSM 的 autoregressive prediction error 随 temporal distance 增大（dt=2 obs_MSE 是 dt=1 的 2-2.75×）。\n      Trained dt_emb (008d) 的 obs gap 看似小 (1.30×) 但具有误导性——\n      其 dt=1 绝对误差本身已是 baseline 的 3× (41.31 vs 13.49)，说明模型整体已崩塌。\n      008d 的 reward gap (2.78×) 最大，因为 trained dt_emb 使 reward head 高度依赖精确的 dt 信息，\n      当 dt>1 prediction 不准确时 reward 误差被放大。\n      008f 的 reward gap (1.01×) 证明没有 dt_embedding 时 reward head 无法区分 dt 值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSSM Fidelity Table (absolute + ratio)\"\n        columns: [\"model\", \"dt1_obs_MSE\", \"dt2_obs_MSE\", \"obs_gap\", \"dt1_reward_MAE\", \"dt2_reward_MAE\", \"reward_gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 13.49, 27.50, \"2.04×\", 0.0102, 0.0159, \"1.56×\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", 41.31, 53.67, \"1.30×\", 0.0568, 0.1579, \"2.78×\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", 8.01, 22.04, \"2.75×\", 0.7469, 0.7526, \"1.01×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RSSM fidelity bar chart — absolute values side-by-side with ratio indicators, avoiding ratio-only misleading interpretation\"\n    analysis: |\n      RSSM fidelity gap 是 CIVO 的 mechanistic foundation。\n      论文必须同时报告绝对误差和比率，避免 008d 的低 obs gap ratio (1.30×) 误导审稿人。\n      关键洞察：trained dt_emb 通过精确 conditioning 让 reward head \"看到\" fidelity gap（reward_gap 2.78×），\n      而 008f 去掉 dt_emb 后 reward head 对 fidelity gap \"视而不见\"（reward_gap 1.01×）。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_031\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy trajectories for healthy vs collapsed configurations to identify collapse signatures.\"\n    expected_results:\n      healthy_configs:\n        008a_s0:\n          entropy_55K: -3.8\n          entropy_105K: -4.9\n          trend: \"gradual stable decline\"\n        008e_v3_s1:\n          entropy_55K: -4.2\n          entropy_105K: -5.1\n          trend: \"gradual stable decline\"\n      civo_collapse:\n        008d_s1:\n          entropy_35K: -3.47\n          entropy_55K: -4.88\n          trend: \"accelerating decrease — policy locks into overestimated actions\"\n      nonCIVO_collapse:\n        008e_v3_s2:\n          entropy_85K: -5.21\n          entropy_105K: -3.83\n          trend: \"reversal — policy destabilizes, entropy increases\"\n      two_signatures_identified: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      两种崩溃路径产生截然不同的 entropy signature：\n      CIVO (Pathway A): critic 高估 value → actor 过度 exploit → policy 变得确定性 → entropy 下降。\n      Non-CIVO (Pathway B): eval 崩塌 → value 滞后 → policy 失去方向 → entropy 上升（策略变随机）。\n      Healthy configs 展示自然的 entropy 下降（策略逐渐确定化），既不锁定也不崩溃。\n      这种 dual-signature 是 C6 \"multiple vulnerability pathways\" 的核心诊断证据。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4-panel actor_entropy comparison — healthy (gradual decline), CIVO (rapid decline → lock-in), non-CIVO (decline then reversal)\"\n    analysis: |\n      Entropy analysis 提供了区分两种崩溃路径的简单诊断工具：\n      entropy 下降 + NVE 上升 = CIVO；entropy 上升 + eval 崩塌 = policy instability。\n      论文 Section 5 Discussion 应用此工具详细阐述 dual-pathway 发现。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: plan_032\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained dt_emb.\"\n    expected_results:\n      008d_trained:\n        value_distribution_shape: \"right-skewed, heavy tail above MC returns\"\n        mean_overestimation: \"+45% above MC return at 35K\"\n        overestimation_growing: true\n      008a_untrained:\n        value_distribution_shape: \"symmetric, centered on MC returns\"\n        mean_bias: \"< 5% of MC return\"\n        calibrated: true\n      baseline:\n        value_distribution_shape: \"slight right skew (normal MBRL overshoot)\"\n        mean_bias: \"~10-15% above MC return (healthy)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trained dt_emb 的 value distribution 系统性偏右（overestimation）因为\n      critic 在 dt>1 imagination steps 看到被放大的 reward predictions，\n      学到的 value function 反映了这些虚高的 imagined returns。\n      Untrained dt_emb 的 value 保持 calibrated 因为不精确的 dt conditioning\n      不会创建系统性偏差——各 imagination step 的误差是随机的，不累积。\n      Distribution 分析比单一 v/e ratio 更 informative，直接回应 R3 审稿关切。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: V(s) vs MC return scatter plots — 008d shows systematic overestimation growing with training, 008a stays calibrated\"\n      - \"Fig: Histogram of (V(s) - MC return) / MC return — 008d right-skewed, 008a centered near zero\"\n    analysis: |\n      如果时间允许，此分析显著加强 C2 evidence。\n      直接回应 R3 (\"v/e ratio is crude proxy\") — distribution 分析提供\n      fine-grained overestimation 证据，而非单一 aggregate ratio。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_033\n    description: \"Track cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 embedding vectors during training.\"\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_similarity_trajectory:\n        init: 0.35\n        10K: 0.28\n        25K: 0.18\n        35K: 0.12\n        55K: 0.08\n        105K: 0.05\n      divergence_onset: \"~10-25K (rapid separation phase)\"\n      divergence_correlates_with_civo: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Training 驱动 dt=1 和 dt=2 embeddings 向不同方向特化——\n      dt=1 embedding 学到的表征对应 accurate single-step predictions，\n      dt=2 embedding 学到的对应 inaccurate multi-step predictions。\n      Cosine similarity 的快速下降（10-25K）与 CIVO onset (25-35K) 在时间上接近，\n      说明 embedding specialization 是 CIVO 的前置条件：\n      只有当 embeddings 足够分离，critic 才能利用精确的 dt conditioning 进行 exploitation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cosine similarity(dt=1, dt=2) over training steps — rapid divergence at 10-25K precedes CIVO onset at 25-35K\"\n    analysis: |\n      这是一个 zero-cost 分析（从已保存的 checkpoints 计算），提供 mechanistic insight。\n      Embedding 分离是 CIVO 的 leading indicator——\n      可用于未来的 early detection / adaptive intervention trigger。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_034\n    description: \"Compute AUROC and classification accuracy across multiple NVE thresholds using all available seeds.\"\n    expected_results:\n      thresholds:\n        1.3x:\n          accuracy: 0.81\n          false_positive_rate: 0.15\n          note: \"too many false positives from transient fluctuations\"\n        1.5x:\n          accuracy: 0.94\n          false_positive_rate: 0.03\n          AUROC: 0.969\n          note: \"near-optimal — captures mechanistic threshold\"\n        1.7x:\n          accuracy: 0.90\n          false_positive_rate: 0.0\n          note: \"misses some self-correcting CIVO cases (e.g., 009b peak 1.62×)\"\n        2.0x:\n          accuracy: 0.84\n          false_positive_rate: 0.0\n          note: \"misses borderline cases\"\n      overall_AUROC: 0.969\n      recommended_threshold: 1.5\n      sample_size: \"15/16 correct at 1.5× across 2 environments\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      1.5× 是 CIVO 正反馈循环的 mechanistic inflection point：\n      当 NVE 超过 1.5× 时，value overestimation 驱动 actor 向 overestimated states 移动\n      的力度超过了 self-correction 机制（value loss gradient pushing value down）的力度。\n      低于 1.5× 的瞬态突破（如 baseline 的 transient fluctuation）通常自行消解。\n      1.3× threshold 引入过多 false positives 因为正常训练 variance 可达 1.2-1.3×。\n      2.0× threshold 遗漏了 self-correcting CIVO 案例（NVE 1.6-1.9× 的 transient breaches）。\n      AUROC 0.969 跨 2 环境表明 NVE 1.5× 是 robust 的跨环境诊断指标。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NVE threshold classification performance\"\n        columns: [\"threshold\", \"accuracy\", \"sensitivity\", \"specificity\", \"F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1.3×\", 0.81, 0.95, 0.70, 0.80]\n          - [\"1.5×\", 0.94, 0.94, 0.94, 0.94]\n          - [\"1.7×\", 0.90, 0.82, 1.00, 0.90]\n          - [\"2.0×\", 0.84, 0.71, 1.00, 0.83]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: ROC curve for NVE threshold CIVO classification — AUROC = 0.969\"\n    analysis: |\n      NVE 1.5× threshold 是论文最强的 quantitative result 之一（C2 的核心 diagnostic marker）。\n      AUROC 0.969 across 2 environments 提供强力证据支持 trained dt_emb → CIVO 的因果链。\n      建议将此分析放在 Section 4 的显著位置，配合 ROC curve 图。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 4: Cartpole Swingup (new environment)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_050\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment, broadening scope beyond locomotion tasks.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_peak: 820\n        eval_converged_200K: 790\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.60-0.72\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_peak: 780\n        eval_converged_200K: 760\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.58-0.70\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_peak: 845\n        eval_converged_200K: 810\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.62-0.74\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        mean_eval_converged: 787\n        std: 21\n        all_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole Swingup 在 DreamerV3 中通常收敛到 ~750-850 range。\n      虽然 observation space 较小（5 dim vs Walker 24 dim），reward structure\n      （swing up + balance）需要精确的 timing control，但 dynamics 比 locomotion 简单。\n      Baseline 应稳定收敛，v/e ratio 在 0.58-0.74 range（与 Walker/Cheetah 一致）。\n      作为 non-locomotion 环境，Cartpole 拓宽了论文的 scope beyond locomotion tasks。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cartpole 3-seed baseline — stable convergence to ~780-810\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole baseline 提供第三个环境的 NVE normalization reference。\n      如果 v/e stable range 与 Walker/Cheetah 一致（~0.6-0.72），\n      说明 DreamerV3 的 value calibration pattern 跨环境稳定，\n      进一步支持 NVE 1.5× 作为 universal diagnostic threshold。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_051\n    description: \"Test CIVO trigger in Cartpole. Simpler dynamics → potentially less severe CIVO.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_peak: 520\n        eval_final_105K: 180\n        nve_peak: 3.8\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 45K\n      seed1:\n        eval_peak: 580\n        eval_final_105K: 550\n        nve_peak: 1.85\n        collapse: false\n        note: \"transient NVE breach, self-correction\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_peak: 490\n        eval_final_105K: 120\n        nve_peak: 5.2\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 55K\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"3/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n        mean_nve_peak: 3.6\n        severity: \"moderate — between Walker (2-4×) and Cheetah (8-108×)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole 的 dynamics 比 Walker 简单（更低维、更少关节），\n      RSSM 的 dt>1 fidelity gap 应该更小 → CIVO severity 中等 (NVE peak 2-6×)，\n      介于 Walker (2-4×) 和 Cheetah (8-108×) 之间。\n      但 mechanism 相同：trained dt_emb → RSSM fidelity gap amplification →\n      value overestimation → CIVO。NVE > 1.5× 应在所有 3 seeds 触发（3/3），\n      collapse 概率 ~50-67%（simpler dynamics 提供略强的 self-correction capacity）。\n      这验证 CIVO 不限于 locomotion tasks——mechanism 是 architecture-specific 而非 task-specific。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment CIVO severity comparison\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"complexity\", \"nve_peak_range\", \"collapse_rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"low\", \"1.8-5.2×\", \"2/3\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"medium\", \"2.0-4.1×\", \"1/2\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"high\", \"5.8-108×\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-environment CIVO severity comparison — NVE severity scales with environment complexity\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole CIVO 验证了 C2 在 non-locomotion 环境的 generality。\n      三个环境的 severity ordering (Cartpole < Walker < Cheetah) 与 RSSM fidelity gap\n      的环境依赖性一致，为 C4 (longer dt amplifies) 提供跨环境证据。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_052\n    description: \"Causal control in Cartpole: no dt_embedding → no CIVO.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_final: 540\n        nve_peak: 0.35\n        collapse: false\n      seed1:\n        eval_final: 510\n        nve_peak: 0.42\n        collapse: false\n      seed2:\n        eval_final: 560\n        nve_peak: 0.30\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        mean_eval_final: 537\n        vs_baseline: \"68% of baseline (537/787)\"\n        nve_max: 0.42\n    result_rationale: |\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 上同样完全阻断 CIVO (0/3)。\n      性能保留率 (68%) 高于 Cheetah (14%) 但低于 Walker (16-55%)——\n      Cartpole 的 reward 对 temporal resolution 的依赖介于两者之间。\n      NVE 一致低于 0.5×，与 Walker 和 Cheetah 的 no-dt-emb 配置模式一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Embedding removal causal control: 3-environment summary\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"CIVO_rate\", \"eval_vs_baseline\", \"nve_max\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"0/4\", \"16-55%\", \"1.41×\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"0/3\", \"14%\", \"0.20×\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"0/3\", \"68%\", \"0.42×\"]\n          - [\"Total\", \"0/10\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-environment embedding removal — 0/10 CIVO across all environments\"\n    analysis: |\n      跨 3 环境 0/10 CIVO → embedding removal 作为 causal control 的 statistical power 极强。\n      与 trained dt_emb 的 8/8 NVE > 1.5× 构成 near-perfect classification。\n      这是 C2 因果论证的 strongest evidence，显著加强了论文的 methodological rigor。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 5: Additional environments and pilot experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: plan_040\n    description: \"Third DMC environment for stronger generalization claim. Hopper Hop requires explosive leg control.\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        seed_eval_range: [180, 280]\n        mean_eval_converged: 230\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.55-0.70\"\n        note: \"Hopper Hop is challenging — DreamerV3 typically reaches 200-300\"\n      trained_dt_emb:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"3/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n        nve_peak_range: [4.0, 40.0]\n        eval_peak_range: [80, 180]\n        severity: \"moderate-high — Hopper dynamics nonlinear\"\n      no_dt_emb:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        eval_range: [50, 100]\n        nve_max: 0.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      Hopper Hop 的动力学高度非线性——单腿跳跃需要精确的 torque timing，\n      微小误差导致 fall over。DreamerV3 baseline 通常在 200-300 range（较低）。\n      RSSM 在 Hopper 的 fidelity gap 应该 moderate-high\n      （比 Walker 复杂因为 contact dynamics 更 discontinuous，但比 Cheetah 简单因为 fewer joints）。\n      Trained dt_emb → CIVO 应触发 (3/3 NVE > 1.5×)，severity 4-40× range。\n      No dt_emb control → 0/3 CIVO，完成 3-environment causal control matrix。\n      作为 P2 优先级，Hopper 主要提供 \"breadth\" 而非新的 mechanistic insight。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Hopper Hop 3-config summary\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"eval_range\", \"CIVO_rate\", \"nve_range\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", \"180-280\", \"0/3\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"80-180 peak, collapse\", \"2/3\", \"4-40×\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"50-100\", \"0/3\", \"<0.5×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Hopper Hop completes the 4-environment CIVO trigger map\"\n    analysis: |\n      Hopper 作为第四个环境将 C1-C2 的 generalization 从 \"2 locomotion + 1 non-locomotion\"\n      扩展到 \"3 locomotion + 1 non-locomotion\"。如果 P2 预算允许，\n      inclusion 显著加强 against R1 (\"limited to one environment\")。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: plan_060\n    description: \"Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination; truncate when exceeding threshold.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_peak: 320\n      eval_final_105K: 280\n      nve_peak: 2.1\n      nve_onset_step: 55K\n      collapse: true\n      collapse_onset: 85K\n      truncation_behavior:\n        mean_truncation_step: \"step 4-5 of 15-step rollout (at dt=2)\"\n        truncation_frequency_at_55K: \"60% of imagination rollouts truncated\"\n        truncation_frequency_at_85K: \"90% of imagination rollouts truncated\"\n      improvement_vs_008d:\n        008d_eval_peak: 167\n        pilot_eval_peak: 320\n        onset_delay: \"+30K steps\"\n        ultimate_outcome: \"still collapses\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      RSSM uncertainty estimation 在训练早期是有用的（truncation 确实截断了高误差的 imagination steps），\n      但存在两个根本局限：\n      (1) RSSM 的 uncertainty 本身在 CIVO regime 下变得不准确——\n          当 representation 被 dt_emb co-adaptation 扭曲时，model 对自身误差的估计也失效。\n      (2) Aggressive truncation 大幅缩短了 effective imagination horizon，\n          相当于将 H=15 降到 H=4-5，严重损伤了 actor-critic 的 learning signal quality。\n      结果是 CIVO onset 延迟 ~30K steps（320 vs 008d 的 167 peak），\n      但最终仍崩溃，因为 uncertainty estimation 的 corruption 使 truncation 失效。\n      作为 P1 pilot，结论是 uncertainty truncation alone 不足——\n      需要与 forward-pass intervention (如 TCN) 结合使用。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Truncation pilot eval + NVE overlay with 008d comparison — delayed onset but eventual collapse\"\n      - \"Fig: Truncation frequency over training — increases from 20% to 90%, indicating model deterioration\"\n    analysis: |\n      Uncertainty truncation 的失败模式与 SGS 类似——\n      它试图在 output/behavior 层面修复 representation-level 的问题。\n      CIVO 的 root cause 在于 trained dt_emb 对 latent representation 的影响，\n      不是 imagination rollout 的长度。这进一步支持 C7/C8 的论证：\n      只有 forward-pass level intervention 才能直接作用于 root cause。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 6: Running C8 experiments (median tier predictions)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"TCN Walker s1 σ=0.2 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_029a_tcn_walker_s1_sigma02\"\n    description: \"Second seed for TCN σ=0.2 on Walker. Current status: 85K steps, eval 152, ve_ratio 0.40.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory_projected:\n        85K: 152\n        95K: 180\n        105K: 210\n        115K: 280\n        125K: 310\n        135K: 340\n        145K: 380\n        155K: 410\n        165K: 430\n        175K: 460\n        185K: 440\n        195K: 420\n        205K: 430\n        215K: 445\n      eval_peak: 460\n      eval_peak_step: 175K\n      eval_last10_mean: 430\n      nve_trajectory_projected:\n        85K: 0.40\n        95K: 0.55\n        105K: 0.65\n        115K: 0.45\n        125K: 0.42\n        135K: 0.38\n        145K: 0.32\n        155K: 0.28\n        165K: 0.25\n        175K: 0.22\n        195K: 0.20\n        215K: 0.18\n      nve_max: 0.65\n      nve_max_step: 105K\n      civo_prevention: true\n      vs_s0_eval_peak: \"460 vs 821 (56%)\"\n      vs_s0_performance_gap: \"significant — s1 recovers slower and lower\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Median 档的核心假设：s1 NVE 保持健康 (< 1.5×) 但 eval peak 显著低于 s0 (< 500 vs 821)。\n      当前 85K 数据（eval 152, ve_ratio 0.40）显示 s1 的学习速度远慢于 s0\n      （s0 在 85K 已达 364, s1 仅 152）。这种差异来自 seed-dependent 的学习动力学：\n      σ=0.2 噪声对 s1 的特定初始化更具破坏性，降低了有效 conditioning precision\n      到 s1 的学习过程无法充分利用时间信息的程度。\n      NVE 保持 < 1.0× 因为噪声确实阻止了 co-adaptation——\n      但代价是 s1 的学习效率显著降低。\n      这证实了 median 假设：noise 防住了 CIVO 但未能维持 baseline-competitive performance——\n      最优 σ 不仅是 environment-specific 还可能是 seed/initialization-specific。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"TCN σ=0.2 Walker per-seed comparison\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_peak\", \"nve_max\", \"prevention\", \"baseline_%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", 821, 0.908, \"Yes\", \"90%\"]\n          - [\"s1 (projected)\", 460, 0.65, \"Yes\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"mean\", 641, 0.78, \"2/2\", \"70%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: TCN σ=0.2 s0 vs s1 eval trajectory — s0 reaches 821 but s1 only ~460\"\n      - \"Fig: per-seed NVE overlay — both below 1.0× but s1 starts higher (more vulnerable)\"\n    analysis: |\n      TCN σ=0.2 在 Walker 上 2/2 prevention（NVE < 1.5×），但性能 variance 大：\n      s0 达 90% baseline 而 s1 仅 ~50%。Per-seed eval peak 在 [460, 821] 范围内，\n      mean ~641（70% baseline）。这比 untreated 008d 好得多（82-268, 9-29%），\n      但不够 robust 来作为 universal recommendation。\n      论文应报告 per-seed variation 并讨论 initialization sensitivity。\n\n  - name: \"TCN Cheetah s0 σ=0.5 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_030b_tcn_cheetah_s0_sigma05\"\n    description: \"TCN on Cheetah with σ=0.5. Current: 16K steps, eval 78.3.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory_projected:\n        15K: 78\n        25K: 160\n        35K: 220\n        45K: 180\n        55K: 130\n        65K: 80\n        75K: 50\n        85K: 30\n        95K: 15\n        105K: 10\n      eval_peak: 220\n      eval_peak_step: 35K\n      nve_55K: 4.5\n      nve_65K: 8.2\n      nve_105K: 15.0\n      nve_max: 15.0\n      civo_prevention: false\n      vs_untreated_cheetah_010b:\n        010b_nve_peak: 70.6\n        tcn_nve_peak: 15.0\n        reduction_factor: \"4.7× (but still >> 1.5×)\"\n        eval_peak_comparison: \"220 vs 248 (similar)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah 的 CIVO severity 是 Walker 的 10-50×（NVE 8-108× vs 2-6×）。\n      σ=0.5 的噪声幅度约为 dt_emb std 的 0.5×——在 Walker 上这已经过量（σ=0.5 Walker NVE peak 4.0），\n      在 Cheetah 上仍然不足。Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 产生的 CIVO 力度\n      远超 σ=0.5 噪声的 damping capacity。\n      结果是 NVE 仍然攀升到 15×（虽然低于 untreated 的 70.6×，reduction ~4.7×），\n      但 15× 远超 1.5× threshold → CIVO 仍然发生。\n      这验证了 median 假设：σ=0.5 不足以覆盖 Cheetah 的 severity gap，\n      需要更大的 σ（可能 σ=2.0-5.0）但过大的 σ 会完全破坏有用信号。\n      这就是 \"narrow band\" problem——optimal σ 可能对 Cheetah 不存在。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"TCN Cheetah σ sensitivity prediction\"\n        columns: [\"σ\", \"nve_max\", \"eval_peak\", \"prevention\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.2 (actual)\", 1.9, 300, \"No (σ insufficient)\"]\n          - [\"0.5 (projected)\", 15.0, 220, \"No (still insufficient)\"]\n          - [\"1.0 (hypothetical)\", 6.0, 100, \"No (destroys signal)\"]\n          - [\"2.0 (hypothetical)\", 2.5, 50, \"No (all signal lost)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah TCN failure — NVE still explodes despite σ=0.5 noise\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-environment TCN comparison — Walker σ=0.2 succeeds vs Cheetah σ=0.5 fails\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah TCN 失败是 median 档的定义性结果。\n      Combined with Walker σ=0.2 success and σ=0.5 failure，结论是：\n      (1) Forward-pass noise 方向正确——TCN 确实 reduces CIVO severity (70.6→15×)\n      (2) 但 reduction 不足以跨 severity threshold\n      (3) Optimal σ 是 environment-specific 且可能不存在 universal value\n      论文 C8 claims 必须加 \"Walker Walk only\" scope 限定。\n\n  - name: \"TCN Walker s0 σ=0.1 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_029c_tcn_walker_s0_sigma01\"\n    description: \"Lower noise test: σ=0.1 on Walker Walk. Currently early stage.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory_projected:\n        25K: 200\n        35K: 280\n        45K: 350\n        55K: 300\n        65K: 250\n        75K: 200\n        85K: 280\n        95K: 320\n        105K: 380\n        115K: 450\n        135K: 500\n        155K: 530\n        175K: 580\n        195K: 560\n        215K: 550\n      eval_peak: 580\n      eval_peak_step: 175K\n      nve_max: 1.65\n      nve_max_step: 65K\n      nve_final: 0.25\n      civo_prevention: false\n      note: \"NVE briefly breaches 1.5× — σ=0.1 provides insufficient noise to prevent transient CIVO\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      σ=0.1 噪声幅度仅为 dt_emb std 的 10%，不足以显著降低 conditioning precision。\n      RSSM 和 critic 仍然可以在噪声背景下提取足够精确的 dt 信号来建立 co-adaptation。\n      NVE 在 55-75K 区间可能短暂突破 1.5×（与 σ=0.2 的 0.908 peak 对比，\n      σ=0.1 的 damping capacity 约为 σ=0.2 的一半）。\n      但因为噪声不为零，CIVO 不会达到 untreated 的严重程度——\n      更像是 \"attenuated CIVO\" 而非 \"prevented CIVO\"。\n      最终可能 self-correct（类似 009b 的轨迹），eval 恢复到 ~550（60% baseline）。\n      σ=0.1 < σ=0.2 < σ=0.5 构成 dose-response：\n      太少 (0.1) → attenuated but not prevented；\n      适中 (0.2) → prevented in Walker；\n      太多 (0.5) → prevented but performance destroyed。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Walker TCN dose-response (σ sweep)\"\n        columns: [\"σ\", \"nve_max\", \"eval_peak\", \"prevention\", \"performance\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (untreated 008d)\", \"4.12\", \"167\", \"No\", \"18%\"]\n          - [\"0.1 (projected)\", \"1.65\", \"580\", \"No (borderline)\", \"63%\"]\n          - [\"0.2 (s0 actual)\", \"0.908\", \"821\", \"Yes\", \"90%\"]\n          - [\"0.2 (s1 projected)\", \"0.65\", \"460\", \"Yes\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"0.5 (s0 actual)\", \"4.0\", \"366\", \"No (oscillatory)\", \"40%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: σ dose-response curve — there is a narrow effective band around σ=0.2 for Walker\"\n    analysis: |\n      σ=0.1 的 borderline 结果进一步确认 optimal σ 的 narrow band 特性。\n      Walker 的 effective σ range 大约是 [0.15, 0.35]，\n      这个 band 的位置和宽度是 environment-specific 的。\n      论文 Section 6 应讨论这一 calibration challenge 并推荐 adaptive σ scheduling。\n\n  - name: \"TCN PickCube s0 σ=0.2 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_031_tcn_pickcube_s0_sigma02\"\n    description: \"TCN on PickCube (manipulation task). Tests cross-task-type generalization.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_peak: 35\n      eval_final: 22\n      nve_peak: 2.8\n      nve_final: 0.08\n      civo_prevention: false\n      pattern: \"transient CIVO → value collapse (similar to exp_019b)\"\n      note: \"PickCube dynamics fundamentally different from locomotion — σ=0.2 not calibrated for this task\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      PickCube 是 manipulation task（抓取并放置），dynamics 与 locomotion 完全不同——\n      contact dynamics 是 discontinuous（抓住/未抓住），reward 是 sparse（成功/失败）。\n      σ=0.2 的校准基于 Walker 的 RSSM fidelity gap profile，对 PickCube 未必适用。\n      PickCube 的 baseline 性能本就较低 (~58-69 eval)，CIVO 表现为\n      transient overestimation → value collapse（与 exp_019b 相似）。\n      TCN 不太可能在 PickCube 上成功，因为：\n      (1) σ=0.2 未针对 manipulation task 校准\n      (2) PickCube 的 CIVO 模式是 transient → value collapse，而非 sustained amplification\n      (3) Sparse reward 环境中 noise 对 learning signal 的破坏更严重\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: PickCube TCN — similar trajectory to untreated exp_019b, TCN ineffective\"\n    analysis: |\n      PickCube TCN 失败（如果确认）进一步支持 median 档的 \"no universal σ\" 结论。\n      但 PickCube 结果应作为 supplementary material 而非 main text，\n      因为 PickCube 的 CIVO 模式本就与 locomotion 不同（transient vs sustained）。\n      论文应 scope C8 claims 为 \"locomotion tasks with sustained CIVO pattern\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52584,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52584},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"372f2b0a-c1ad-449c-a9d8-bf3ae2bed5bf","uuid":"25ca0604-b90b-4f2b-82de-ada67524a9cd"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":700106,"duration_api_ms":701892,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Median 档核心叙事：C1-C7 诊断主线完全成立（31+ 配置、2+ 环境），C8 降级为 \"exploratory forward-pass intervention\"。\n  TCN σ=0.2 在 Walker Walk 上是项目首个完全预防 CIVO 的干预（s0 NVE 全程 < 1.0×，eval peak 821），\n  但 s1 eval peak 显著低于 s0（< 500），Cheetah σ=0.5 失败（NVE 3-20×）。\n  最优 σ 是 environment-specific 且 narrow band（σ=0.1 不足、σ=0.5 过量、σ=0.2 仅 Walker 有效），\n  无 universal σ 存在。Forward-pass principle 方向正确但实现需要 adaptive calibration（超出本文 scope）。\n  \n  叙事重心移回诊断：SGS 全面失败（C7, 1/17 across 3 variants）+ TCN Walker 成功 + TCN Cheetah 失败\n  共同构成 \"干预难度梯度\"——backward-pass (SGS) < forward-pass uniform noise (TCN) < (future) adaptive forward-pass。\n  C8 标题从 \"forward-pass intervention\" 改为 \"exploratory forward-pass intervention\"，\n  所有 TCN 结论加 \"Walker Walk only\" scope 限定，Cheetah 失败作为 \"calibration challenge\" 呈现。\n  \n  Running experiments 预测：\n  - exp_029a (TCN Walker s1 σ=0.2)：NVE 保持 < 1.5×，eval peak ~450（远低于 s0 的 821），prevention 成功但性能不可泛化\n  - exp_030b (TCN Cheetah s0 σ=0.5)：NVE 3-15×，eval peak ~120-200，Cheetah severity gap 无法被 σ=0.5 覆盖\n  - exp_029c (TCN Walker s0 σ=0.1)：NVE 可能 breach 1.5×（噪声不足），eval peak ~300-500\n  - exp_031 (TCN PickCube s0 σ=0.2)：预计 negative——PickCube 动力学与 locomotion 差异大，σ=0.2 未必适用\n  \n  Paper claims：C1-C7 fully supported (7 claims)，C8 partial (scoped to Walker proof-of-concept)。\n  CoRL reviewer 可能要求补充 environment 或 challenge robustness——准备 rebuttal 强调诊断贡献独立于 C8。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 1: Walker Walk diagnostic replications (C1-C7)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO trigger with 2 additional independent seeds. 008d config: dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 155\n          25K: 170\n          35K: 150\n          45K: 143\n          55K: 85\n          65K: 245\n          75K: 180\n          85K: 200\n          95K: 135\n          105K: 130\n        eval_peak: 245\n        eval_peak_step: 65K\n        eval_final: 130\n        nve_25K: 1.78\n        nve_35K: 1.71\n        nve_45K: 2.09\n        nve_55K: 4.12\n        nve_peak: 4.12\n        nve_peak_step: 55K\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_type: \"classic CIVO (value-driven, entropy decreasing)\"\n        collapse_onset: 25K\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 39\n          15K: 144\n          25K: 141\n          35K: 164\n          45K: 141\n          55K: 172\n          65K: 209\n          75K: 197\n          85K: 236\n          95K: 279\n          105K: 268\n        eval_peak: 279\n        eval_peak_step: 95K\n        eval_final: 268\n        nve_25K: 2.05\n        nve_35K: 1.24\n        nve_45K: 1.62\n        nve_55K: 1.41\n        nve_65K: 0.94\n        nve_75K: 0.66\n        nve_85K: 0.51\n        nve_95K: 0.43\n        nve_105K: 0.38\n        nve_peak: 2.05\n        nve_peak_step: 25K\n        collapse: false\n        collapse_type: \"transient CIVO, self-correction\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"2/2 seeds\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n        nve_threshold_separating_power: \"maintained — both seeds exceed 1.5× at some point\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trained dt_emb 可靠地诱导 NVE > 1.5×（2/2 seeds），因为 RSSM 在 dt>1 的 fidelity gap\n      通过精确的 dt_embedding conditioning 被放大为系统性 reward overestimation。\n      Collapse 是 stochastic 的（1/2），取决于训练早期的随机性（权重初始化、mini-batch 采样序列）\n      是否让 NVE 跨过 \"point of no return\" threshold 从而锁定正反馈循环。\n      Seed 2 在 45K 后 NVE 开始下降（1.62→0.38），展示了 value self-correction——\n      early stochasticity 使其避开了持续 overestimation 的轨迹。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d cross-seed NVE comparison\"\n        columns: [\"step\", \"seed1_nve\", \"seed2_nve\", \"pathological_threshold\"]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 1.78, 2.05, 1.5]\n          - [35K, 1.71, 1.24, 1.5]\n          - [45K, 2.09, 1.62, 1.5]\n          - [55K, 4.12, 1.41, 1.5]\n          - [105K, \"collapsed\", 0.38, 1.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig A: 008d seed 1 vs seed 2 eval trajectory — seed 1 collapses at 55K while seed 2 shows slow recovery to 268\"\n      - \"Fig B: NVE trajectory overlay — both exceed 1.5× early, seed 1 accelerates (sustained), seed 2 self-corrects (transient)\"\n    analysis: |\n      C2 因果方向在两个独立 seed 上复现。NVE > 1.5× threshold 的 separating power\n      从 4/4 (原始) 维持。关键新增发现：value self-correction mechanism (seed 2)\n      的存在说明 CIVO 不是 deterministic collapse 而是 stochastic bifurcation——\n      early training dynamics 决定 sustained vs transient 轨迹。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: \"Replicate causal control (no dt_embedding → no CIVO) with additional seeds.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 30\n          15K: 165\n          25K: 195\n          35K: 210\n          45K: 190\n          55K: 175\n          65K: 370\n          75K: 320\n          85K: 250\n          95K: 320\n          105K: 500\n        eval_peak: 500\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 500\n        nve_max_35kplus: 1.02\n        nve_105K: 0.30\n        collapse: false\n        reward_MAE: 0.75\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 30\n          15K: 157\n          25K: 169\n          35K: 179\n          45K: 211\n          55K: 239\n          65K: 244\n          75K: 359\n          85K: 227\n          95K: 191\n          105K: 148\n        eval_peak: 359\n        eval_peak_step: 75K\n        eval_final: 148\n        nve_max_35kplus: 1.26\n        nve_105K: 1.14\n        collapse: false\n        pattern: \"peak-then-decline, no CIVO but poor late performance\"\n      seed3:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 148\n          25K: 180\n          35K: 220\n          45K: 255\n          55K: 300\n          65K: 280\n          75K: 310\n          85K: 350\n          95K: 290\n          105K: 312\n        eval_peak: 350\n        eval_peak_step: 85K\n        eval_final: 312\n        nve_max_35kplus: 0.85\n        nve_105K: 0.52\n        collapse: false\n      seed4:\n        eval_peak: 488\n        eval_final: 307\n        nve_peak: 1.41\n        nve_105K: 0.58\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"0/4 seeds\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/4\"\n        eval_range_105K: \"[148, 500]\"\n        mean_nve_105K: 0.64\n    result_rationale: |\n      去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2（reward gap 仅 1.01× vs 008d 的 2.78×），\n      reward_MAE 升至 baseline 75×。CIVO 反馈循环被完全阻断——critic 无法利用精确的 dt 信号\n      进行 value exploitation。所有 seed 的 NVE 保持 < 1.5×（最高 1.26×，瞬态）。\n      但性能受限（eval 148-500 vs baseline 916）因为模型丧失了所有时间信息编码能力。\n      Seed 间高 variance（148-500）反映了无时间信息条件下的学习不稳定性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"No-dt-emb causal control: 4-seed summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_peak\", \"eval_105K\", \"nve_peak\", \"nve_105K\", \"CIVO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 500, 500, 1.02, 0.30, \"No\"]\n          - [2, 359, 148, 1.26, 1.14, \"No\"]\n          - [3, 350, 312, 0.85, 0.52, \"No\"]\n          - [4, 488, 307, 1.41, 0.58, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 008f 4-seed NVE overlay — all seeds remain below 1.5× threshold (dashed line), contrasting sharply with 008d's 2/2 breaches\"\n    analysis: |\n      因果控制在 4 seeds 上 100% 复现（0/4 CIVO）。与 008d 的对比：trained dt_emb 2/2 exceed 1.5×，\n      no dt_emb 0/4 exceed 1.5× → 6/6 perfect classification on this pair。\n      008f 的角色是因果控制实验（非推荐方案），证明 dt_embedding conditioning 是 CIVO 的 necessary condition。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_013\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with unexposed dt_emb (trained but only on dt=1 data). Subsample OFF + H=15.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 167\n          25K: 140\n          35K: 394\n          45K: 414\n          55K: 441\n          65K: 492\n          75K: 452\n          85K: 547\n          95K: 629\n          105K: 631\n        eval_peak: 631\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 631\n        nve_105K: 0.43\n        civo_alert: 0\n        pattern: \"slow but steady climb, no zigzag\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 175\n          25K: 280\n          35K: 410\n          45K: 380\n          55K: 608\n          65K: 654\n          75K: 534\n          85K: 605\n          95K: 819\n          105K: 899\n        eval_peak: 899\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 899\n        nve_105K: 0.33\n        civo_alert: 0\n        pattern: \"strong recovery, near-baseline performance\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"0/2\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/2\"\n        eval_range_105K: \"[631, 899]\"\n        mean_eval_105K: 765\n        vs_baseline_105K: \"-5% to -31%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Unexposed dt_emb（trained 但仅见过 dt=1 数据）保留了有用的时间表征但无法被 dt>1 exploitation。\n      因为 subsample OFF 意味着训练数据全部是 dt=1 transitions，dt_embedding 学到的是 dt=1 的表征——\n      当 imagination 用 dt=2 时，embedding 提供的是不精确的（dt=1-tuned）信号，\n      critic 无法建立精确 dt>1 conditioning → CIVO 反馈循环无法启动。\n      Value growth 被抑制在 baseline 水平以下（NVE 0.33-0.43×），性能保留 69-98% baseline。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Unexposed dt_emb: value suppression evidence\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_105K\", \"nve_105K\", \"vs_baseline\", \"pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, 0.59, \"-15.1%\", \"zigzag two-cycle recovery\"]\n          - [1, 631, 0.43, \"-31.1%\", \"slow steady climb\"]\n          - [2, 899, 0.33, \"-1.8%\", \"strong recovery\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-seed 008a eval trajectory — all show recovery patterns (zigzag or steady), none collapse\"\n      - \"Fig: NVE overlay — all seeds maintain NVE < 1.0× at 105K, confirming structural value suppression\"\n    analysis: |\n      C3 在 3 seeds (含原始 s0) 上确认：unexposed dt_emb 可靠抑制 value overestimation (0/3 CIVO)。\n      性能范围 631-899 (69-98% baseline) 远优于 008f (148-500, 16-55%)，\n      说明保留 dt_embedding 架构但不暴露于 dt>1 数据是更优的 value protection 策略。\n      Seed 间 variance (631 vs 899) 反映了正常的 RL 训练随机性，非系统性问题。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: plan_014\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination with trained dt_emb. Tests whether restricting imagination prevents collapse.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 131\n          25K: 156\n          35K: 276\n          45K: 382\n          55K: 487\n          65K: 581\n          75K: 574\n          85K: 657\n          95K: 852\n          105K: 870\n        eval_peak: 870\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        nve_stable_range: \"0.72-0.80×\"\n        nve_peak: 0.80\n        collapse: false\n        gate_dt_mean: 1.0\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 39\n          15K: 181\n          25K: 212\n          35K: 320\n          45K: 357\n          55K: 418\n          65K: 435\n          75K: 577\n          85K: 715\n          95K: 452\n          105K: 137\n        eval_peak: 715\n        eval_peak_step: 85K\n        eval_final: 137\n        nve_85K: 0.68\n        nve_95K: 1.34\n        nve_105K: 3.78\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: 95K\n        collapse_type: \"non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy increasing)\"\n        actor_entropy_85K: -5.21\n        actor_entropy_105K: -3.83\n        gate_dt_mean: 1.0\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n        c6_status: \"PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      dt=1 imagination 消除了 CIVO Pathway A（value 驱动的 overestimation），seed 1 因此健康（NVE 0.80×）。\n      但 trained dt_emb 在 dt>1 训练数据上学到的表征会改变 RSSM 的 latent space 结构——\n      即使 imagination 限制为 dt=1，被 dt>1 训练数据 \"污染\" 的表征仍可能导致\n      Pathway B（eval 驱动的 policy instability）。Seed 2 的崩溃动力学与经典 CIVO 定性不同：\n      value 温和变化 (+13%→-12%) 而 eval 暴跌 (-81%)，actor entropy 上升（策略变随机）——\n      这是 policy destabilization 而非 critic exploitation。\n      Collapse rate 1/2 与 008d (1/2) 相同，说明 dt=1 imagination 未降低总崩溃概率，\n      只是将机制从 CIVO 切换为 non-CIVO policy instability。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 dual-pathway collapse comparison\"\n        columns: [\"feature\", \"008d_s1_CIVO\", \"008e_v3_s2_nonCIVO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"value change\", \"+130% (60→138)\", \"+13% (339→384)\"]\n          - [\"eval change\", \"-43% (146→83)\", \"-81% (715→137)\"]\n          - [\"NVE driver\", \"value numerator explosion\", \"eval denominator collapse\"]\n          - [\"actor_entropy\", \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\", \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\"]\n          - [\"mechanism\", \"critic overestimate → actor exploit\", \"eval crash → value lags\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 008e_v3 seed 1 (healthy) vs seed 2 (collapsed) eval trajectories with baseline overlay\"\n      - \"Fig: actor_entropy comparison — CIVO pathway (008d) shows entropy decrease vs non-CIVO (008e_v3_s2) shows entropy increase\"\n    analysis: |\n      C6 partially falsified: dt=1 imagination 不能阻止崩溃 (1/2 seeds)。\n      但崩溃机制与经典 CIVO 不同 → trained dt_embedding 通过多条路径创造脆弱性。\n      009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定 (618→596→836)，排除 seed 脆弱假说。\n      论文表述：dt=1 imagination eliminates CIVO (Pathway A) but not all failure modes。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: plan_015\n    description: \"Freeze dt_embedding (requires_grad=False), random init. Diagnoses whether dt_emb TRAINING is the necessary condition for CIVO.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory:\n        5K: 31\n        15K: 168\n        25K: 172\n        35K: 202\n        45K: 122\n        55K: 106\n        65K: 160\n        75K: 80\n        85K: 184\n        95K: 238\n        105K: 204\n      eval_peak: 238\n      eval_peak_step: 95K\n      eval_final: 204\n      nve_85K: 0.47\n      nve_95K: 0.39\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n      value_mean_105K: 56.2\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      collapse: false\n      collapse_mechanism: \"gradient starvation from frozen dt_emb\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      冻结 dt_emb 阻止了训练驱动的 co-adaptation → NVE 保持健康 (0.39-0.47×)，远低于 1.5× 阈值。\n      但冻结的随机 embedding 向 RSSM 注入持续的无信息噪声信号，模型必须学会忽略它。\n      这导致 actor_loss → 0（梯度饥饿）：value landscape 在 embedding-conditioned states 周围变得平坦，\n      actor 无法获得有效的梯度信号来改进策略。性能严重受限（204 vs baseline 916, 22%）。\n      关键诊断结论：dt_emb 的 TRAINING 是 CIVO 的必要条件——冻结 (015b) 和移除 (008f) 都阻止了 CIVO，\n      但各自引入不同的性能损伤机制（梯度饥饿 vs reward 预测失败）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 dt_emb intervention matrix\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"dt_emb_status\", \"CIVO\", \"eval_105K\", \"mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d\", \"trained + active\", \"Yes (2/2)\", \"82-268\", \"CIVO feedback loop\"]\n          - [\"008a\", \"trained + unexposed\", \"No (0/3)\", \"631-899\", \"value suppression\"]\n          - [\"015b\", \"frozen (random)\", \"No (0/1)\", \"204\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"008f\", \"removed (dim=0)\", \"No (0/4)\", \"148-500\", \"reward prediction failure\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4-config comparison showing eval trajectories and NVE — only trained+active shows CIVO\"\n    analysis: |\n      015b 与 008d、008a、008f 构成完整的 2×2 消融矩阵。\n      只有 \"trained + active\" 配置触发 CIVO，确认 dt_emb 的训练过程（而非其存在本身）是 necessary condition。\n      这支持 C2 的 mechanistic claim：训练过程使 dt_emb 学到精确但错误的 dt>1 conditioning，\n      而非 dt_emb 的架构存在本身导致问题。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: plan_016\n    description: \"Narrow 008e_v3 collapse probability estimate from 1/2 to x/4.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 35\n          15K: 145\n          25K: 195\n          35K: 310\n          45K: 380\n          55K: 440\n          65K: 460\n          75K: 510\n          85K: 520\n          95K: 320\n          105K: 93\n        eval_peak: 520\n        eval_peak_step: 85K\n        eval_final: 93\n        nve_peak: 4.02\n        nve_peak_step: 105K\n        collapse: true\n        collapse_onset: \"85-95K\"\n        collapse_type: \"hybrid — eval-driven with moderate value acceleration\"\n      seed4:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 38\n          15K: 160\n          25K: 200\n          35K: 330\n          45K: 420\n          55K: 510\n          65K: 600\n          75K: 640\n          85K: 720\n          95K: 830\n          105K: 899\n        eval_peak: 899\n        eval_peak_step: 105K\n        eval_final: 899\n        nve_peak: 0.99\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        total_collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n        collapsed_seeds: [2, 3]\n        healthy_seeds: [1, 4]\n        collapse_probability_estimate: \"50% ± 25% (binomial CI)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      4 seeds 中 2 个崩溃（50%），与 008d 的 50% 崩溃率一致。\n      dt=1 imagination 确实消除了 CIVO Pathway A，但 Pathway B（eval-driven policy instability）\n      的基准崩溃概率仍然是 ~50%，与 dt=2 imagination 下的 CIVO 崩溃概率没有显著差异。\n      这说明 trained dt_emb 的脆弱性不仅在于 imagination 中的 dt>1 使用，\n      而在于训练数据中 dt>1 transitions 对 latent representation 的全局影响。\n      Healthy seeds (1, 4) 达到 870-899 (95-98% baseline)，说明当 Pathway B 不触发时，\n      dt=1 imagination 配置的性能上限接近 baseline。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 4-seed collapse summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_105K\", \"nve_peak\", \"collapsed\", \"pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 870, 0.80, \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [2, 137, 3.78, \"Yes\", \"B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [3, 93, 4.02, \"Yes\", \"B (hybrid)\"]\n          - [4, 899, 0.99, \"No\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4-seed 008e_v3 eval trajectory overlay — bimodal outcome (850-900 vs <140)\"\n      - \"Fig: collapse probability comparison: 008d (1/2 CIVO) vs 008e_v3 (2/4 non-CIVO) — rates indistinguishable\"\n    analysis: |\n      2/4 崩溃率的 binomial 95% CI = [12%, 88%]，与 008d 的 50% 无法区分。\n      但两种配置的崩溃机制定性不同（CIVO vs non-CIVO）。\n      论文结论：trained dt_embedding 创造 ~50% 崩溃概率，与 imagination dt 设定无关。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 2: Cheetah Run replications\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_020\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment for v/e calibration and cross-environment generalization.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_peak: 625\n        eval_final_200K: 625\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.55-0.70\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_peak: 573\n        eval_final_200K: 520\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.50-0.70\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_peak: 645\n        eval_final_200K: 645\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.55-0.70\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        mean_eval_final: 597\n        std_eval_final: 55\n        ve_ratio_converged: \"0.50-0.70\"\n        all_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah Run baseline 在 DreamerV3 中稳定收敛到 ~520-650 range（低于 Walker 的 ~950），\n      因为 Cheetah 的 locomotion dynamics 更复杂——需要协调更多关节来维持前进速度，\n      且 reward 是 velocity-based 而非 position-based。\n      v/e ratio 收敛到 0.50-0.70，与 Walker baseline (0.69-0.72) 类似但略低，\n      反映了 Cheetah 的 higher return variance 降低了 value prediction 的 calibration 精度。\n      所有 3 seeds 稳定，无 CIVO（dt=1 configuration）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah 3-seed baseline overlay — all converge to 520-650 range\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah baseline 为后续 CIVO 实验提供 NVE normalization 参考。\n      Mean ~597 比 Walker ~930 低 36%——Cheetah 是更 challenging 的环境，\n      这会放大 CIVO severity（因为 RSSM prediction 在更复杂动力学下的 fidelity gap 更大）。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_021\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO trigger in Cheetah Run. Expect severe CIVO due to wider RSSM fidelity gap.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 8\n          15K: 80\n          25K: 180\n          35K: 248\n          45K: 200\n          55K: 120\n          65K: 45\n          75K: 20\n          85K: 5\n          95K: 1\n          105K: 1\n        eval_peak: 248\n        eval_peak_step: 35K\n        nve_65K: 8.3\n        nve_105K: 70.6\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 45K\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 10\n          15K: 95\n          25K: 220\n          35K: 310\n          45K: 280\n          55K: 170\n          65K: 80\n          75K: 30\n          85K: 15\n          95K: 52\n          105K: 52\n        eval_peak: 310\n        eval_peak_step: 35K\n        nve_55K: 5.8\n        nve_105K: 12.4\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 45K\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 9\n          15K: 70\n          25K: 150\n          35K: 230\n          45K: 150\n          55K: 60\n          65K: 25\n          75K: 10\n          85K: 3\n          95K: 1\n          105K: 1\n        eval_peak: 230\n        eval_peak_step: 35K\n        nve_65K: 15.2\n        nve_105K: 108\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 55K\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"3/3\"\n        nve_range: \"[5.8, 108]\"\n        eval_peak_range: \"[230, 310]\"\n        severity_vs_walker: \"~10-50× more severe NVE\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 比 Walker 大得多——Cheetah 的 dynamics 更非线性\n      （多关节协调 + velocity reward），dt>1 prediction error 更大。\n      Trained dt_emb 提供精确但严重错误的 dt>1 conditioning →\n      value overestimation 幅度是 Walker 的 10-50×（Walker NVE 2-6× vs Cheetah 8-108×）。\n      所有 3 seeds 崩溃，因为 Cheetah 的 severity 足够高，使得 self-correction 的概率极低——\n      即使早期 stochasticity 有利，强大的正反馈循环也会在 45-55K 内压倒 self-correction 机制。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CIVO severity cross-environment comparison\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"nve_range\", \"collapse_rate\", \"onset_step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2.0-4.1×\", \"1/2 (50%)\", \"25-35K\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"5.8-108×\", \"3/3 (100%)\", \"45-55K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah 3-seed CIVO cascade — all collapse within 35-55K, NVE explodes to 10-100× range\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-environment NVE severity comparison (log scale) — Cheetah 1-2 orders of magnitude worse\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah 的 100% collapse rate (3/3) vs Walker 的 50% (1/2) 确认 CIVO severity\n      是 environment-dependent 的。RSSM fidelity gap 在复杂动力学环境中被放大，\n      导致 CIVO 正反馈循环更强、self-correction 概率更低。\n      这为 C8 的 TCN calibration challenge 提供机制解释——\n      σ=0.2 足以 dampen Walker 的 2-6× NVE 但不足以对抗 Cheetah 的 8-108×。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_022\n    description: \"Causal control: no dt_embedding in Cheetah. Expect no CIVO but severe reward prediction degradation.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_final: 97\n        nve_peak: 0.20\n        collapse: false\n        reward_MAE: \">0.8\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_final: 77\n        eval_peak: 130\n        nve_peak: 0.10\n        collapse: false\n      seed2:\n        eval_final: 85\n        eval_peak: 110\n        nve_peak: 0.18\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        mean_eval_final: 86\n        vs_baseline: \"14.4% of baseline (86/597)\"\n        nve_max: 0.20\n    result_rationale: |\n      与 Walker 008f 相同的机制：移除 dt_embedding 完全阻断 CIVO 反馈循环（0/3 CIVO），\n      但 reward head 丧失时间分辨能力（reward_MAE > baseline 50×）。\n      Cheetah 的 velocity-based reward 对时间信息更敏感——\n      没有 dt 信息时 reward head 无法区分 \"前进一步\" 和 \"前进两步\" 的奖励差异，\n      导致 eval 仅达 baseline 的 14%（Walker 008f 达 16-55%）。\n      NVE 极低 (0.10-0.20×) 因为 critic 严重低估 value（缺乏 reward 信号）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah no-dt-emb 3-seed eval — flat at 77-97, far below baseline 597 but no collapse\"\n    analysis: |\n      Embedding removal 在 Cheetah 上同样 100% 阻止 CIVO (0/3)，与 Walker (0/4) 一致。\n      跨两个环境 0/7 CIVO → removal 是 sufficient condition for CIVO prevention。\n      性能损伤在 Cheetah 更严重（14% vs Walker 16-55%），\n      因为 Cheetah 的 reward structure 对 temporal resolution 的依赖更强。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_023\n    description: \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah. Unexposed dt_emb should maintain near-baseline performance.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_final_105K: 532\n        nve_105K: 0.49\n        collapse: false\n      seed1:\n        eval_final_105K: 504\n        nve_105K: 0.48\n        collapse: false\n      seed2:\n        eval_final_105K: 520\n        nve_105K: 0.45\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        mean_eval: 519\n        vs_baseline: \"86.9% of baseline (519/597)\"\n        nve_range: \"0.45-0.49\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      与 Walker 008a 相同的机制：unexposed dt_emb 保留了有用的 dt=1 表征能力，\n      同时因为未暴露于 dt>1 数据而无法被 exploitation。\n      Cheetah 的性能保留率 (87%) 与 Walker (69-98%) 一致。\n      NVE 一致低于 0.5×，确认 value suppression 机制跨环境有效。\n      这是 Cheetah 上性能最好的非 baseline 配置（519 vs 008f 的 86 vs 008d 的 <52）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah configuration comparison\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"mean_eval\", \"vs_baseline\", \"CIVO_rate\", \"mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", \"597\", \"100%\", \"0/3\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"008a (unexposed)\", \"519\", \"87%\", \"0/3\", \"value suppression\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"86\", \"14%\", \"0/3\", \"reward prediction failure\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", \"<52\", \"<9%\", \"3/3\", \"CIVO collapse\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah 4-config eval comparison — unexposed dt_emb is the only viable non-baseline configuration\"\n    analysis: |\n      Unexposed dt_emb 在 Cheetah 上同样是最优的 CIVO-free 配置，\n      性能保留 87% baseline（vs 008f 的 14%）。\n      跨 Walker + Cheetah，unexposed dt_emb 一致提供 strong value protection\n      + high performance retention → 推荐 practical guideline。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 3: Analysis experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: plan_030\n    description: \"Quantify RSSM fidelity gap across dt values from existing trained models.\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 13.49\n        dt2_obs_mse: 27.50\n        obs_gap_ratio: 2.04\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0102\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.0159\n        reward_gap_ratio: 1.56\n      008d_trained:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 41.31\n        dt2_obs_mse: 53.67\n        obs_gap_ratio: 1.30\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.0568\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.1579\n        reward_gap_ratio: 2.78\n      008f_no_dtEmb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 8.01\n        dt2_obs_mse: 22.04\n        obs_gap_ratio: 2.75\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.7469\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.7526\n        reward_gap_ratio: 1.01\n    result_rationale: |\n      RSSM 的 autoregressive prediction error 随 temporal distance 增大（dt=2 obs_MSE 是 dt=1 的 2-2.75×）。\n      Trained dt_emb (008d) 的 obs gap 看似小 (1.30×) 但具有误导性——\n      其 dt=1 绝对误差本身已是 baseline 的 3× (41.31 vs 13.49)，说明模型整体已崩塌。\n      008d 的 reward gap (2.78×) 最大，因为 trained dt_emb 使 reward head 高度依赖精确的 dt 信息，\n      当 dt>1 prediction 不准确时 reward 误差被放大。\n      008f 的 reward gap (1.01×) 证明没有 dt_embedding 时 reward head 无法区分 dt 值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSSM Fidelity Table (absolute + ratio)\"\n        columns: [\"model\", \"dt1_obs_MSE\", \"dt2_obs_MSE\", \"obs_gap\", \"dt1_reward_MAE\", \"dt2_reward_MAE\", \"reward_gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 13.49, 27.50, \"2.04×\", 0.0102, 0.0159, \"1.56×\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", 41.31, 53.67, \"1.30×\", 0.0568, 0.1579, \"2.78×\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", 8.01, 22.04, \"2.75×\", 0.7469, 0.7526, \"1.01×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: RSSM fidelity bar chart — absolute values side-by-side with ratio indicators, avoiding ratio-only misleading interpretation\"\n    analysis: |\n      RSSM fidelity gap 是 CIVO 的 mechanistic foundation。\n      论文必须同时报告绝对误差和比率，避免 008d 的低 obs gap ratio (1.30×) 误导审稿人。\n      关键洞察：trained dt_emb 通过精确 conditioning 让 reward head \"看到\" fidelity gap（reward_gap 2.78×），\n      而 008f 去掉 dt_emb 后 reward head 对 fidelity gap \"视而不见\"（reward_gap 1.01×）。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_031\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy trajectories for healthy vs collapsed configurations to identify collapse signatures.\"\n    expected_results:\n      healthy_configs:\n        008a_s0:\n          entropy_55K: -3.8\n          entropy_105K: -4.9\n          trend: \"gradual stable decline\"\n        008e_v3_s1:\n          entropy_55K: -4.2\n          entropy_105K: -5.1\n          trend: \"gradual stable decline\"\n      civo_collapse:\n        008d_s1:\n          entropy_35K: -3.47\n          entropy_55K: -4.88\n          trend: \"accelerating decrease — policy locks into overestimated actions\"\n      nonCIVO_collapse:\n        008e_v3_s2:\n          entropy_85K: -5.21\n          entropy_105K: -3.83\n          trend: \"reversal — policy destabilizes, entropy increases\"\n      two_signatures_identified: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      两种崩溃路径产生截然不同的 entropy signature：\n      CIVO (Pathway A): critic 高估 value → actor 过度 exploit → policy 变得确定性 → entropy 下降。\n      Non-CIVO (Pathway B): eval 崩塌 → value 滞后 → policy 失去方向 → entropy 上升（策略变随机）。\n      Healthy configs 展示自然的 entropy 下降（策略逐渐确定化），既不锁定也不崩溃。\n      这种 dual-signature 是 C6 \"multiple vulnerability pathways\" 的核心诊断证据。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4-panel actor_entropy comparison — healthy (gradual decline), CIVO (rapid decline → lock-in), non-CIVO (decline then reversal)\"\n    analysis: |\n      Entropy analysis 提供了区分两种崩溃路径的简单诊断工具：\n      entropy 下降 + NVE 上升 = CIVO；entropy 上升 + eval 崩塌 = policy instability。\n      论文 Section 5 Discussion 应用此工具详细阐述 dual-pathway 发现。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: plan_032\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained dt_emb.\"\n    expected_results:\n      008d_trained:\n        value_distribution_shape: \"right-skewed, heavy tail above MC returns\"\n        mean_overestimation: \"+45% above MC return at 35K\"\n        overestimation_growing: true\n      008a_untrained:\n        value_distribution_shape: \"symmetric, centered on MC returns\"\n        mean_bias: \"< 5% of MC return\"\n        calibrated: true\n      baseline:\n        value_distribution_shape: \"slight right skew (normal MBRL overshoot)\"\n        mean_bias: \"~10-15% above MC return (healthy)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trained dt_emb 的 value distribution 系统性偏右（overestimation）因为\n      critic 在 dt>1 imagination steps 看到被放大的 reward predictions，\n      学到的 value function 反映了这些虚高的 imagined returns。\n      Untrained dt_emb 的 value 保持 calibrated 因为不精确的 dt conditioning\n      不会创建系统性偏差——各 imagination step 的误差是随机的，不累积。\n      Distribution 分析比单一 v/e ratio 更 informative，直接回应 R3 审稿关切。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: V(s) vs MC return scatter plots — 008d shows systematic overestimation growing with training, 008a stays calibrated\"\n      - \"Fig: Histogram of (V(s) - MC return) / MC return — 008d right-skewed, 008a centered near zero\"\n    analysis: |\n      如果时间允许，此分析显著加强 C2 evidence。\n      直接回应 R3 (\"v/e ratio is crude proxy\") — distribution 分析提供\n      fine-grained overestimation 证据，而非单一 aggregate ratio。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_033\n    description: \"Track cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 embedding vectors during training.\"\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_similarity_trajectory:\n        init: 0.35\n        10K: 0.28\n        25K: 0.18\n        35K: 0.12\n        55K: 0.08\n        105K: 0.05\n      divergence_onset: \"~10-25K (rapid separation phase)\"\n      divergence_correlates_with_civo: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Training 驱动 dt=1 和 dt=2 embeddings 向不同方向特化——\n      dt=1 embedding 学到的表征对应 accurate single-step predictions，\n      dt=2 embedding 学到的对应 inaccurate multi-step predictions。\n      Cosine similarity 的快速下降（10-25K）与 CIVO onset (25-35K) 在时间上接近，\n      说明 embedding specialization 是 CIVO 的前置条件：\n      只有当 embeddings 足够分离，critic 才能利用精确的 dt conditioning 进行 exploitation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cosine similarity(dt=1, dt=2) over training steps — rapid divergence at 10-25K precedes CIVO onset at 25-35K\"\n    analysis: |\n      这是一个 zero-cost 分析（从已保存的 checkpoints 计算），提供 mechanistic insight。\n      Embedding 分离是 CIVO 的 leading indicator——\n      可用于未来的 early detection / adaptive intervention trigger。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: plan_034\n    description: \"Compute AUROC and classification accuracy across multiple NVE thresholds using all available seeds.\"\n    expected_results:\n      thresholds:\n        1.3x:\n          accuracy: 0.81\n          false_positive_rate: 0.15\n          note: \"too many false positives from transient fluctuations\"\n        1.5x:\n          accuracy: 0.94\n          false_positive_rate: 0.03\n          AUROC: 0.969\n          note: \"near-optimal — captures mechanistic threshold\"\n        1.7x:\n          accuracy: 0.90\n          false_positive_rate: 0.0\n          note: \"misses some self-correcting CIVO cases (e.g., 009b peak 1.62×)\"\n        2.0x:\n          accuracy: 0.84\n          false_positive_rate: 0.0\n          note: \"misses borderline cases\"\n      overall_AUROC: 0.969\n      recommended_threshold: 1.5\n      sample_size: \"15/16 correct at 1.5× across 2 environments\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      1.5× 是 CIVO 正反馈循环的 mechanistic inflection point：\n      当 NVE 超过 1.5× 时，value overestimation 驱动 actor 向 overestimated states 移动\n      的力度超过了 self-correction 机制（value loss gradient pushing value down）的力度。\n      低于 1.5× 的瞬态突破（如 baseline 的 transient fluctuation）通常自行消解。\n      1.3× threshold 引入过多 false positives 因为正常训练 variance 可达 1.2-1.3×。\n      2.0× threshold 遗漏了 self-correcting CIVO 案例（NVE 1.6-1.9× 的 transient breaches）。\n      AUROC 0.969 跨 2 环境表明 NVE 1.5× 是 robust 的跨环境诊断指标。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NVE threshold classification performance\"\n        columns: [\"threshold\", \"accuracy\", \"sensitivity\", \"specificity\", \"F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1.3×\", 0.81, 0.95, 0.70, 0.80]\n          - [\"1.5×\", 0.94, 0.94, 0.94, 0.94]\n          - [\"1.7×\", 0.90, 0.82, 1.00, 0.90]\n          - [\"2.0×\", 0.84, 0.71, 1.00, 0.83]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: ROC curve for NVE threshold CIVO classification — AUROC = 0.969\"\n    analysis: |\n      NVE 1.5× threshold 是论文最强的 quantitative result 之一（C2 的核心 diagnostic marker）。\n      AUROC 0.969 across 2 environments 提供强力证据支持 trained dt_emb → CIVO 的因果链。\n      建议将此分析放在 Section 4 的显著位置，配合 ROC curve 图。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 4: Cartpole Swingup (new environment)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_050\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment, broadening scope beyond locomotion tasks.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_peak: 820\n        eval_converged_200K: 790\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.60-0.72\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_peak: 780\n        eval_converged_200K: 760\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.58-0.70\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_peak: 845\n        eval_converged_200K: 810\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.62-0.74\"\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        mean_eval_converged: 787\n        std: 21\n        all_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole Swingup 在 DreamerV3 中通常收敛到 ~750-850 range。\n      虽然 observation space 较小（5 dim vs Walker 24 dim），reward structure\n      （swing up + balance）需要精确的 timing control，但 dynamics 比 locomotion 简单。\n      Baseline 应稳定收敛，v/e ratio 在 0.58-0.74 range（与 Walker/Cheetah 一致）。\n      作为 non-locomotion 环境，Cartpole 拓宽了论文的 scope beyond locomotion tasks。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cartpole 3-seed baseline — stable convergence to ~780-810\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole baseline 提供第三个环境的 NVE normalization reference。\n      如果 v/e stable range 与 Walker/Cheetah 一致（~0.6-0.72），\n      说明 DreamerV3 的 value calibration pattern 跨环境稳定，\n      进一步支持 NVE 1.5× 作为 universal diagnostic threshold。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_051\n    description: \"Test CIVO trigger in Cartpole. Simpler dynamics → potentially less severe CIVO.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_peak: 520\n        eval_final_105K: 180\n        nve_peak: 3.8\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 45K\n      seed1:\n        eval_peak: 580\n        eval_final_105K: 550\n        nve_peak: 1.85\n        collapse: false\n        note: \"transient NVE breach, self-correction\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_peak: 490\n        eval_final_105K: 120\n        nve_peak: 5.2\n        collapse: true\n        civo_onset: 55K\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"3/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n        mean_nve_peak: 3.6\n        severity: \"moderate — between Walker (2-4×) and Cheetah (8-108×)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole 的 dynamics 比 Walker 简单（更低维、更少关节），\n      RSSM 的 dt>1 fidelity gap 应该更小 → CIVO severity 中等 (NVE peak 2-6×)，\n      介于 Walker (2-4×) 和 Cheetah (8-108×) 之间。\n      但 mechanism 相同：trained dt_emb → RSSM fidelity gap amplification →\n      value overestimation → CIVO。NVE > 1.5× 应在所有 3 seeds 触发（3/3），\n      collapse 概率 ~50-67%（simpler dynamics 提供略强的 self-correction capacity）。\n      这验证 CIVO 不限于 locomotion tasks——mechanism 是 architecture-specific 而非 task-specific。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment CIVO severity comparison\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"complexity\", \"nve_peak_range\", \"collapse_rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"low\", \"1.8-5.2×\", \"2/3\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"medium\", \"2.0-4.1×\", \"1/2\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"high\", \"5.8-108×\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-environment CIVO severity comparison — NVE severity scales with environment complexity\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole CIVO 验证了 C2 在 non-locomotion 环境的 generality。\n      三个环境的 severity ordering (Cartpole < Walker < Cheetah) 与 RSSM fidelity gap\n      的环境依赖性一致，为 C4 (longer dt amplifies) 提供跨环境证据。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: plan_052\n    description: \"Causal control in Cartpole: no dt_embedding → no CIVO.\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_final: 540\n        nve_peak: 0.35\n        collapse: false\n      seed1:\n        eval_final: 510\n        nve_peak: 0.42\n        collapse: false\n      seed2:\n        eval_final: 560\n        nve_peak: 0.30\n        collapse: false\n      cross_seed_summary:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        mean_eval_final: 537\n        vs_baseline: \"68% of baseline (537/787)\"\n        nve_max: 0.42\n    result_rationale: |\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 上同样完全阻断 CIVO (0/3)。\n      性能保留率 (68%) 高于 Cheetah (14%) 但低于 Walker (16-55%)——\n      Cartpole 的 reward 对 temporal resolution 的依赖介于两者之间。\n      NVE 一致低于 0.5×，与 Walker 和 Cheetah 的 no-dt-emb 配置模式一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Embedding removal causal control: 3-environment summary\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"CIVO_rate\", \"eval_vs_baseline\", \"nve_max\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"0/4\", \"16-55%\", \"1.41×\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"0/3\", \"14%\", \"0.20×\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"0/3\", \"68%\", \"0.42×\"]\n          - [\"Total\", \"0/10\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-environment embedding removal — 0/10 CIVO across all environments\"\n    analysis: |\n      跨 3 环境 0/10 CIVO → embedding removal 作为 causal control 的 statistical power 极强。\n      与 trained dt_emb 的 8/8 NVE > 1.5× 构成 near-perfect classification。\n      这是 C2 因果论证的 strongest evidence，显著加强了论文的 methodological rigor。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 5: Additional environments and pilot experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: plan_040\n    description: \"Third DMC environment for stronger generalization claim. Hopper Hop requires explosive leg control.\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        seed_eval_range: [180, 280]\n        mean_eval_converged: 230\n        ve_ratio_stable: \"0.55-0.70\"\n        note: \"Hopper Hop is challenging — DreamerV3 typically reaches 200-300\"\n      trained_dt_emb:\n        nve_exceeds_1_5x: \"3/3\"\n        collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n        nve_peak_range: [4.0, 40.0]\n        eval_peak_range: [80, 180]\n        severity: \"moderate-high — Hopper dynamics nonlinear\"\n      no_dt_emb:\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        eval_range: [50, 100]\n        nve_max: 0.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      Hopper Hop 的动力学高度非线性——单腿跳跃需要精确的 torque timing，\n      微小误差导致 fall over。DreamerV3 baseline 通常在 200-300 range（较低）。\n      RSSM 在 Hopper 的 fidelity gap 应该 moderate-high\n      （比 Walker 复杂因为 contact dynamics 更 discontinuous，但比 Cheetah 简单因为 fewer joints）。\n      Trained dt_emb → CIVO 应触发 (3/3 NVE > 1.5×)，severity 4-40× range。\n      No dt_emb control → 0/3 CIVO，完成 3-environment causal control matrix。\n      作为 P2 优先级，Hopper 主要提供 \"breadth\" 而非新的 mechanistic insight。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Hopper Hop 3-config summary\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"eval_range\", \"CIVO_rate\", \"nve_range\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", \"180-280\", \"0/3\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"80-180 peak, collapse\", \"2/3\", \"4-40×\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"50-100\", \"0/3\", \"<0.5×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Hopper Hop completes the 4-environment CIVO trigger map\"\n    analysis: |\n      Hopper 作为第四个环境将 C1-C2 的 generalization 从 \"2 locomotion + 1 non-locomotion\"\n      扩展到 \"3 locomotion + 1 non-locomotion\"。如果 P2 预算允许，\n      inclusion 显著加强 against R1 (\"limited to one environment\")。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: plan_060\n    description: \"Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination; truncate when exceeding threshold.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_peak: 320\n      eval_final_105K: 280\n      nve_peak: 2.1\n      nve_onset_step: 55K\n      collapse: true\n      collapse_onset: 85K\n      truncation_behavior:\n        mean_truncation_step: \"step 4-5 of 15-step rollout (at dt=2)\"\n        truncation_frequency_at_55K: \"60% of imagination rollouts truncated\"\n        truncation_frequency_at_85K: \"90% of imagination rollouts truncated\"\n      improvement_vs_008d:\n        008d_eval_peak: 167\n        pilot_eval_peak: 320\n        onset_delay: \"+30K steps\"\n        ultimate_outcome: \"still collapses\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      RSSM uncertainty estimation 在训练早期是有用的（truncation 确实截断了高误差的 imagination steps），\n      但存在两个根本局限：\n      (1) RSSM 的 uncertainty 本身在 CIVO regime 下变得不准确——\n          当 representation 被 dt_emb co-adaptation 扭曲时，model 对自身误差的估计也失效。\n      (2) Aggressive truncation 大幅缩短了 effective imagination horizon，\n          相当于将 H=15 降到 H=4-5，严重损伤了 actor-critic 的 learning signal quality。\n      结果是 CIVO onset 延迟 ~30K steps（320 vs 008d 的 167 peak），\n      但最终仍崩溃，因为 uncertainty estimation 的 corruption 使 truncation 失效。\n      作为 P1 pilot，结论是 uncertainty truncation alone 不足——\n      需要与 forward-pass intervention (如 TCN) 结合使用。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Truncation pilot eval + NVE overlay with 008d comparison — delayed onset but eventual collapse\"\n      - \"Fig: Truncation frequency over training — increases from 20% to 90%, indicating model deterioration\"\n    analysis: |\n      Uncertainty truncation 的失败模式与 SGS 类似——\n      它试图在 output/behavior 层面修复 representation-level 的问题。\n      CIVO 的 root cause 在于 trained dt_emb 对 latent representation 的影响，\n      不是 imagination rollout 的长度。这进一步支持 C7/C8 的论证：\n      只有 forward-pass level intervention 才能直接作用于 root cause。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Group 6: Running C8 experiments (median tier predictions)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"TCN Walker s1 σ=0.2 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_029a_tcn_walker_s1_sigma02\"\n    description: \"Second seed for TCN σ=0.2 on Walker. Current status: 85K steps, eval 152, ve_ratio 0.40.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory_projected:\n        85K: 152\n        95K: 180\n        105K: 210\n        115K: 280\n        125K: 310\n        135K: 340\n        145K: 380\n        155K: 410\n        165K: 430\n        175K: 460\n        185K: 440\n        195K: 420\n        205K: 430\n        215K: 445\n      eval_peak: 460\n      eval_peak_step: 175K\n      eval_last10_mean: 430\n      nve_trajectory_projected:\n        85K: 0.40\n        95K: 0.55\n        105K: 0.65\n        115K: 0.45\n        125K: 0.42\n        135K: 0.38\n        145K: 0.32\n        155K: 0.28\n        165K: 0.25\n        175K: 0.22\n        195K: 0.20\n        215K: 0.18\n      nve_max: 0.65\n      nve_max_step: 105K\n      civo_prevention: true\n      vs_s0_eval_peak: \"460 vs 821 (56%)\"\n      vs_s0_performance_gap: \"significant — s1 recovers slower and lower\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Median 档的核心假设：s1 NVE 保持健康 (< 1.5×) 但 eval peak 显著低于 s0 (< 500 vs 821)。\n      当前 85K 数据（eval 152, ve_ratio 0.40）显示 s1 的学习速度远慢于 s0\n      （s0 在 85K 已达 364, s1 仅 152）。这种差异来自 seed-dependent 的学习动力学：\n      σ=0.2 噪声对 s1 的特定初始化更具破坏性，降低了有效 conditioning precision\n      到 s1 的学习过程无法充分利用时间信息的程度。\n      NVE 保持 < 1.0× 因为噪声确实阻止了 co-adaptation——\n      但代价是 s1 的学习效率显著降低。\n      这证实了 median 假设：noise 防住了 CIVO 但未能维持 baseline-competitive performance——\n      最优 σ 不仅是 environment-specific 还可能是 seed/initialization-specific。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"TCN σ=0.2 Walker per-seed comparison\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval_peak\", \"nve_max\", \"prevention\", \"baseline_%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", 821, 0.908, \"Yes\", \"90%\"]\n          - [\"s1 (projected)\", 460, 0.65, \"Yes\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"mean\", 641, 0.78, \"2/2\", \"70%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: TCN σ=0.2 s0 vs s1 eval trajectory — s0 reaches 821 but s1 only ~460\"\n      - \"Fig: per-seed NVE overlay — both below 1.0× but s1 starts higher (more vulnerable)\"\n    analysis: |\n      TCN σ=0.2 在 Walker 上 2/2 prevention（NVE < 1.5×），但性能 variance 大：\n      s0 达 90% baseline 而 s1 仅 ~50%。Per-seed eval peak 在 [460, 821] 范围内，\n      mean ~641（70% baseline）。这比 untreated 008d 好得多（82-268, 9-29%），\n      但不够 robust 来作为 universal recommendation。\n      论文应报告 per-seed variation 并讨论 initialization sensitivity。\n\n  - name: \"TCN Cheetah s0 σ=0.5 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_030b_tcn_cheetah_s0_sigma05\"\n    description: \"TCN on Cheetah with σ=0.5. Current: 16K steps, eval 78.3.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory_projected:\n        15K: 78\n        25K: 160\n        35K: 220\n        45K: 180\n        55K: 130\n        65K: 80\n        75K: 50\n        85K: 30\n        95K: 15\n        105K: 10\n      eval_peak: 220\n      eval_peak_step: 35K\n      nve_55K: 4.5\n      nve_65K: 8.2\n      nve_105K: 15.0\n      nve_max: 15.0\n      civo_prevention: false\n      vs_untreated_cheetah_010b:\n        010b_nve_peak: 70.6\n        tcn_nve_peak: 15.0\n        reduction_factor: \"4.7× (but still >> 1.5×)\"\n        eval_peak_comparison: \"220 vs 248 (similar)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah 的 CIVO severity 是 Walker 的 10-50×（NVE 8-108× vs 2-6×）。\n      σ=0.5 的噪声幅度约为 dt_emb std 的 0.5×——在 Walker 上这已经过量（σ=0.5 Walker NVE peak 4.0），\n      在 Cheetah 上仍然不足。Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 产生的 CIVO 力度\n      远超 σ=0.5 噪声的 damping capacity。\n      结果是 NVE 仍然攀升到 15×（虽然低于 untreated 的 70.6×，reduction ~4.7×），\n      但 15× 远超 1.5× threshold → CIVO 仍然发生。\n      这验证了 median 假设：σ=0.5 不足以覆盖 Cheetah 的 severity gap，\n      需要更大的 σ（可能 σ=2.0-5.0）但过大的 σ 会完全破坏有用信号。\n      这就是 \"narrow band\" problem——optimal σ 可能对 Cheetah 不存在。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"TCN Cheetah σ sensitivity prediction\"\n        columns: [\"σ\", \"nve_max\", \"eval_peak\", \"prevention\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.2 (actual)\", 1.9, 300, \"No (σ insufficient)\"]\n          - [\"0.5 (projected)\", 15.0, 220, \"No (still insufficient)\"]\n          - [\"1.0 (hypothetical)\", 6.0, 100, \"No (destroys signal)\"]\n          - [\"2.0 (hypothetical)\", 2.5, 50, \"No (all signal lost)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Cheetah TCN failure — NVE still explodes despite σ=0.5 noise\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-environment TCN comparison — Walker σ=0.2 succeeds vs Cheetah σ=0.5 fails\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah TCN 失败是 median 档的定义性结果。\n      Combined with Walker σ=0.2 success and σ=0.5 failure，结论是：\n      (1) Forward-pass noise 方向正确——TCN 确实 reduces CIVO severity (70.6→15×)\n      (2) 但 reduction 不足以跨 severity threshold\n      (3) Optimal σ 是 environment-specific 且可能不存在 universal value\n      论文 C8 claims 必须加 \"Walker Walk only\" scope 限定。\n\n  - name: \"TCN Walker s0 σ=0.1 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_029c_tcn_walker_s0_sigma01\"\n    description: \"Lower noise test: σ=0.1 on Walker Walk. Currently early stage.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_trajectory_projected:\n        25K: 200\n        35K: 280\n        45K: 350\n        55K: 300\n        65K: 250\n        75K: 200\n        85K: 280\n        95K: 320\n        105K: 380\n        115K: 450\n        135K: 500\n        155K: 530\n        175K: 580\n        195K: 560\n        215K: 550\n      eval_peak: 580\n      eval_peak_step: 175K\n      nve_max: 1.65\n      nve_max_step: 65K\n      nve_final: 0.25\n      civo_prevention: false\n      note: \"NVE briefly breaches 1.5× — σ=0.1 provides insufficient noise to prevent transient CIVO\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      σ=0.1 噪声幅度仅为 dt_emb std 的 10%，不足以显著降低 conditioning precision。\n      RSSM 和 critic 仍然可以在噪声背景下提取足够精确的 dt 信号来建立 co-adaptation。\n      NVE 在 55-75K 区间可能短暂突破 1.5×（与 σ=0.2 的 0.908 peak 对比，\n      σ=0.1 的 damping capacity 约为 σ=0.2 的一半）。\n      但因为噪声不为零，CIVO 不会达到 untreated 的严重程度——\n      更像是 \"attenuated CIVO\" 而非 \"prevented CIVO\"。\n      最终可能 self-correct（类似 009b 的轨迹），eval 恢复到 ~550（60% baseline）。\n      σ=0.1 < σ=0.2 < σ=0.5 构成 dose-response：\n      太少 (0.1) → attenuated but not prevented；\n      适中 (0.2) → prevented in Walker；\n      太多 (0.5) → prevented but performance destroyed。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Walker TCN dose-response (σ sweep)\"\n        columns: [\"σ\", \"nve_max\", \"eval_peak\", \"prevention\", \"performance\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (untreated 008d)\", \"4.12\", \"167\", \"No\", \"18%\"]\n          - [\"0.1 (projected)\", \"1.65\", \"580\", \"No (borderline)\", \"63%\"]\n          - [\"0.2 (s0 actual)\", \"0.908\", \"821\", \"Yes\", \"90%\"]\n          - [\"0.2 (s1 projected)\", \"0.65\", \"460\", \"Yes\", \"50%\"]\n          - [\"0.5 (s0 actual)\", \"4.0\", \"366\", \"No (oscillatory)\", \"40%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: σ dose-response curve — there is a narrow effective band around σ=0.2 for Walker\"\n    analysis: |\n      σ=0.1 的 borderline 结果进一步确认 optimal σ 的 narrow band 特性。\n      Walker 的 effective σ range 大约是 [0.15, 0.35]，\n      这个 band 的位置和宽度是 environment-specific 的。\n      论文 Section 6 应讨论这一 calibration challenge 并推荐 adaptive σ scheduling。\n\n  - name: \"TCN PickCube s0 σ=0.2 (running — median prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"registry: exp_031_tcn_pickcube_s0_sigma02\"\n    description: \"TCN on PickCube (manipulation task). Tests cross-task-type generalization.\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_peak: 35\n      eval_final: 22\n      nve_peak: 2.8\n      nve_final: 0.08\n      civo_prevention: false\n      pattern: \"transient CIVO → value collapse (similar to exp_019b)\"\n      note: \"PickCube dynamics fundamentally different from locomotion — σ=0.2 not calibrated for this task\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      PickCube 是 manipulation task（抓取并放置），dynamics 与 locomotion 完全不同——\n      contact dynamics 是 discontinuous（抓住/未抓住），reward 是 sparse（成功/失败）。\n      σ=0.2 的校准基于 Walker 的 RSSM fidelity gap profile，对 PickCube 未必适用。\n      PickCube 的 baseline 性能本就较低 (~58-69 eval)，CIVO 表现为\n      transient overestimation → value collapse（与 exp_019b 相似）。\n      TCN 不太可能在 PickCube 上成功，因为：\n      (1) σ=0.2 未针对 manipulation task 校准\n      (2) PickCube 的 CIVO 模式是 transient → value collapse，而非 sustained amplification\n      (3) Sparse reward 环境中 noise 对 learning signal 的破坏更严重\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: PickCube TCN — similar trajectory to untreated exp_019b, TCN ineffective\"\n    analysis: |\n      PickCube TCN 失败（如果确认）进一步支持 median 档的 \"no universal σ\" 结论。\n      但 PickCube 结果应作为 supplementary material 而非 main text，\n      因为 PickCube 的 CIVO 模式本就与 locomotion 不同（transient vs sustained）。\n      论文应 scope C8 claims 为 \"locomotion tasks with sustained CIVO pattern\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"372f2b0a-c1ad-449c-a9d8-bf3ae2bed5bf","total_cost_usd":1.3298245,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52584,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":37928,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52584,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":37928,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52584},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":47141,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.047241000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":37928,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":52584,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2825834999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6329b8c5-e773-4bb5-b277-99db535977a6"}
